{"jobs":[{"id":"4793f5c8-009a-418e-b33f-1c2ae892f070","title":"Senior Software Engineer I","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"APAC - India","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-03T13:11:10.952+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Karnataka","addressCountry":"India","addressLocality":"Bangalore"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/4793f5c8-009a-418e-b33f-1c2ae892f070","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/4793f5c8-009a-418e-b33f-1c2ae892f070/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.</p><h2><strong>Summary</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security is looking for a Senior Software Engineer to join our growing development team. In this role, you'll design, build, and operate Menlo services, working closely with product, security, and operations partners to ship reliable, high-performing systems. The ideal candidate has hands-on experience building software in a cloud computing environment and is comfortable owning a feature from design through production. The team uses AI-assisted development tools — including AI pair-programming assistants and AI-assisted code review — as a standard part of the engineering workflow, and you'll be expected to use them to work faster and more effectively.</p><h2><strong>Outcomes &amp; KPIs</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Outcome(s) Owned:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable, on-time delivery of new features and services that scale with Menlo's distributed platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Sustained reliability and performance of the services this role owns or contributes to.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Success Metrics / KPIs:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">On-time delivery of committed features/services against sprint and quarterly roadmap commitments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Uptime/availability of owned services (e.g., 99.9%+)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reduction in P1/P2 production incidents tied to owned services</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Code review turnaround time and PR cycle time</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mean time to resolution (MTTR) for production issues in owned systems</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, develop, and own new features and services that are key contributors to Menlo's technical roadmap</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate and implement development and deployment technologies for API design, highly available and scalable distributed systems, and multithreaded/asynchronous applications with performance and security in mind</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build, deploy, and operate core components of the Menlo Security platform</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use AI pair-programming and AI-assisted code-review tools to accelerate implementation, generate tests, and speed up review cycles</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Apply AI-assisted debugging tooling to diagnose issues in distributed systems more quickly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with product, security, operations, and other cross-functional stakeholders to align on requirements and schedules</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Functional Competencies</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Required:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3-4 years of experience in cloud computing or related technical fields, with hands-on backend development in one or more languages such as Python, Go, C++, or Node.js</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solid experience with Linux and networking technologies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with core AWS services (e.g., EC2, S3, VPC) or GCP and standard software development tooling (e.g., Git, Jira, Confluence, Jenkins)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with complex data structures, databases, and analytics technologies (e.g., Redis, Postgres, MySQL, Druid)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written and verbal communication skills, with high attention to detail and documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Self-directed and motivated to learn new technologies with minimal guidance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">BE/<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://B.Tech\">B.Tech</a> or Master's degree required</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred / Nice to Have:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Linux boot processes, service monitoring, and networking internals (e.g., Tornado, C/C++, Go, systemd, Monit, Bash, cgroups/runc/libcontainer, Docker)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience adapting and improving engineering best practices such as test-driven development, continuous delivery, and scrum/automation practices</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable incorporating AI-assisted coding tools (e.g., AI pair-programming assistants, AI code-review tools) into a modern development workflow</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">MSGL-I4</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/\">LinkedIn</a>!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why Menlo?</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: <strong>Proactive Leadership</strong>, <strong>Straight Talk</strong>, <strong>United Impact</strong>, <strong>Elevated Talent</strong>, and <strong>Customer-Compelled</strong>. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability</strong>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>TO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.</strong></em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.\n\n\nSUMMARY\n\nMenlo Security is looking for a Senior Software Engineer to join our growing development team. In this role, you'll design, build, and operate Menlo services, working closely with product, security, and operations partners to ship reliable, high-performing systems. The ideal candidate has hands-on experience building software in a cloud computing environment and is comfortable owning a feature from design through production. The team uses AI-assisted development tools — including AI pair-programming assistants and AI-assisted code review — as a standard part of the engineering workflow, and you'll be expected to use them to work faster and more effectively.\n\n\nOUTCOMES & KPIS\n\nKey Outcome(s) Owned:\n\n - Reliable, on-time delivery of new features and services that scale with Menlo's distributed platform.\n\n - Sustained reliability and performance of the services this role owns or contributes to.\n\nSuccess Metrics / KPIs:\n\n - On-time delivery of committed features/services against sprint and quarterly roadmap commitments\n\n - Uptime/availability of owned services (e.g., 99.9%+)\n\n - Reduction in P1/P2 production incidents tied to owned services\n\n - Code review turnaround time and PR cycle time\n\n - Mean time to resolution (MTTR) for production issues in owned systems\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Design, develop, and own new features and services that are key contributors to Menlo's technical roadmap\n\n - Evaluate and implement development and deployment technologies for API design, highly available and scalable distributed systems, and multithreaded/asynchronous applications with performance and security in mind\n\n - Build, deploy, and operate core components of the Menlo Security platform\n\n - Use AI pair-programming and AI-assisted code-review tools to accelerate implementation, generate tests, and speed up review cycles\n\n - Apply AI-assisted debugging tooling to diagnose issues in distributed systems more quickly\n\n - Partner with product, security, operations, and other cross-functional stakeholders to align on requirements and schedules\n\n\nFUNCTIONAL COMPETENCIES\n\nRequired:\n\n - 3-4 years of experience in cloud computing or related technical fields, with hands-on backend development in one or more languages such as Python, Go, C++, or Node.js\n\n - Solid experience with Linux and networking technologies\n\n - Experience with core AWS services (e.g., EC2, S3, VPC) or GCP and standard software development tooling (e.g., Git, Jira, Confluence, Jenkins)\n\n - Experience with complex data structures, databases, and analytics technologies (e.g., Redis, Postgres, MySQL, Druid)\n\n - Strong written and verbal communication skills, with high attention to detail and documentation\n\n - Self-directed and motivated to learn new technologies with minimal guidance\n\n - BE/B.Tech http://B.Tech or Master's degree required\n\nPreferred / Nice to Have:\n\n - Experience with Linux boot processes, service monitoring, and networking internals (e.g., Tornado, C/C++, Go, systemd, Monit, Bash, cgroups/runc/libcontainer, Docker)\n\n - Experience adapting and improving engineering best practices such as test-driven development, continuous delivery, and scrum/automation practices\n\n - Comfortable incorporating AI-assisted coding tools (e.g., AI pair-programming assistants, AI code-review tools) into a modern development workflow\n\n\n\nMSGL-I4\n\nFollow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/!\n\nWhy Menlo?\n\nAt Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: Proactive Leadership, Straight Talk, United Impact, Elevated Talent, and Customer-Compelled. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.\n\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability.\n\nTO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"6d39fd97-f731-453c-99ef-8331eca78749","title":"Sales Engineer - Channel","department":"Sales","team":"Sales Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"APAC - Japan","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2025-09-25T16:42:39.289+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Kanto","addressCountry":"Japan","addressLocality":"Tokyo"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/6d39fd97-f731-453c-99ef-8331eca78749","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/6d39fd97-f731-453c-99ef-8331eca78749/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security Channel Sales Engineer is a channel-focused, highly technical sales professional who provides support and guidance to channel partners, while collaborating with Channel Account Managers and channel organizations to recommend and develop appropriate security-focused solution offerings. The SE acts in a consultative fashion and is looked to as an expert in the IT security field by the channel team, channel partners and customers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Articulate the benefits of Menlo Security products and services for both technical and non-technical audiences. Research technical requirements of a channel-led opportunity to scope and architect a solution that meets the customer’s needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understand the customer's business drivers and map them to Menlo Security products and services that meet both their needs and budget.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support Proof of Concept (POC) engagements on channel-led opportunities. This includes deployment, configuration and troubleshooting of Menlo Security products and services, training of individuals on the use of Menlo Security products and services, acting as an interface between channel partners and Menlo Security's technical staff to lead the POC engagements to success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide reporting and feedback on channel partners and field activities to Sales, Product Management and Engineering.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with channel partners to enable partner self-sufficiency and drive channel-led opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with channel partners to grow and expand the implementation and integration of Menlo Security products and services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support channel-led marketing campaigns and events.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's or master's degree in computer science or related discipline or equivalent experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ year experience in sales engineering role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent knowledge and experience in deployment, configuration and troubleshooting of a wide variety of IT security technologies and solutions, especially the following fucus areas:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Web Technologies and Security (HTTP(S), Proxy, TLS Inspection, URL Filtering, Anti-Virus, Sandbox)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Email Technologies and Security (SMTP(S), SPF/DKIM/DMARC, Anti-Spam, Anti-Virus, Sandbox)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Network Technologies and Security (OSI Model, TCP/IP, IPv4/IPv6, DNS, Routing, Switching, Subnetting, VLAN, Tap, Load Balancing, Firewall, IPS/IDS, VPN)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Other Technologies and Security (DLP, CASB, SIEM, EDR/NDR/XDR, SOAR)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Malware Analysis (Static and Dynamic)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Digital Forensics and Incident Response (Host-based and Network-based)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enterprise Architecture (Active Directory, ADFS, SCCM, LDAP, RADIUS, TACACS+, SAML, MFA, PKI)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Virtualization Technologies (VMware, Citrix, Hyper-V, KVM)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cloud Computing Services (GCP, AWS, Azure)</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent knowledge and experience in maintaining sales engagement processes and progress in SFDC.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent knowledge and experience in managing technical responses to RFIs/RFPs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluent reading, writing and speaking skills in Japanese and English.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Overnight travel throughout Japan and other countries (mainly USA) is required.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong leadership skills with the ability to independently prioritize and execute project tasks in a methodical and disciplined manner. Set and manage expectations with senior stakeholders and team members.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional written and oral communication skills. This role requires an ability to understand and articulate both the business benefits (value proposition) and technical advantages of Menlo Security products and services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understand and be conversant about Menlo Security competitors, their solutions, strengths, weaknesses, opportunities and threats.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with various hacking and exploitation tools and methodologies, common malware families, and evasion techniques.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hold cybersecurity certifications such as ISC2, GIAC, IPA.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hold English certifications of Eiken Grade Pre-1+, TOEIC 800+ or equivalent.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>Please note that this role requires the candidate to be based in Tokyo, and relocation sponsorship is not available.</strong></em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/\">LinkedIn</a>!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why Menlo?</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: <strong>Proactive Leadership</strong>, <strong>Straight Talk</strong>, <strong>United Impact</strong>, <strong>Elevated Talent</strong>, and <strong>Customer-Compelled</strong>. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability</strong>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>TO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.</strong></em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.\n\nMenlo Security Channel Sales Engineer is a channel-focused, highly technical sales professional who provides support and guidance to channel partners, while collaborating with Channel Account Managers and channel organizations to recommend and develop appropriate security-focused solution offerings. The SE acts in a consultative fashion and is looked to as an expert in the IT security field by the channel team, channel partners and customers.\n\nResponsibilities\n\n - Articulate the benefits of Menlo Security products and services for both technical and non-technical audiences. Research technical requirements of a channel-led opportunity to scope and architect a solution that meets the customer’s needs.\n\n - Understand the customer's business drivers and map them to Menlo Security products and services that meet both their needs and budget.\n\n - Support Proof of Concept (POC) engagements on channel-led opportunities. This includes deployment, configuration and troubleshooting of Menlo Security products and services, training of individuals on the use of Menlo Security products and services, acting as an interface between channel partners and Menlo Security's technical staff to lead the POC engagements to success.\n\n - Provide reporting and feedback on channel partners and field activities to Sales, Product Management and Engineering.\n\n - Work closely with channel partners to enable partner self-sufficiency and drive channel-led opportunities.\n\n - Work closely with channel partners to grow and expand the implementation and integration of Menlo Security products and services.\n\n - Support channel-led marketing campaigns and events.\n\nRequirements\n\n - Bachelor's or master's degree in computer science or related discipline or equivalent experience.\n\n - 5+ year experience in sales engineering role.\n\n - Excellent knowledge and experience in deployment, configuration and troubleshooting of a wide variety of IT security technologies and solutions, especially the following fucus areas:\n   \n   - Web Technologies and Security (HTTP(S), Proxy, TLS Inspection, URL Filtering, Anti-Virus, Sandbox)\n   \n   - Email Technologies and Security (SMTP(S), SPF/DKIM/DMARC, Anti-Spam, Anti-Virus, Sandbox)\n   \n   - Network Technologies and Security (OSI Model, TCP/IP, IPv4/IPv6, DNS, Routing, Switching, Subnetting, VLAN, Tap, Load Balancing, Firewall, IPS/IDS, VPN)\n   \n   - Other Technologies and Security (DLP, CASB, SIEM, EDR/NDR/XDR, SOAR)\n   \n   - Malware Analysis (Static and Dynamic)\n   \n   - Digital Forensics and Incident Response (Host-based and Network-based)\n   \n   - Enterprise Architecture (Active Directory, ADFS, SCCM, LDAP, RADIUS, TACACS+, SAML, MFA, PKI)\n   \n   - Virtualization Technologies (VMware, Citrix, Hyper-V, KVM)\n   \n   - Cloud Computing Services (GCP, AWS, Azure)\n\n - Excellent knowledge and experience in maintaining sales engagement processes and progress in SFDC.\n\n - Excellent knowledge and experience in managing technical responses to RFIs/RFPs.\n\n - Fluent reading, writing and speaking skills in Japanese and English.\n\n - Overnight travel throughout Japan and other countries (mainly USA) is required.\n\nAdditional Qualifications\n\n - Strong leadership skills with the ability to independently prioritize and execute project tasks in a methodical and disciplined manner. Set and manage expectations with senior stakeholders and team members.\n\n - Exceptional written and oral communication skills. This role requires an ability to understand and articulate both the business benefits (value proposition) and technical advantages of Menlo Security products and services.\n\n - Understand and be conversant about Menlo Security competitors, their solutions, strengths, weaknesses, opportunities and threats.\n\n - Familiarity with various hacking and exploitation tools and methodologies, common malware families, and evasion techniques.\n\n - Hold cybersecurity certifications such as ISC2, GIAC, IPA.\n\n - Hold English certifications of Eiken Grade Pre-1+, TOEIC 800+ or equivalent.\n   \n   \n   \n   Please note that this role requires the candidate to be based in Tokyo, and relocation sponsorship is not available.\n   \n   \n\nFollow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/!\n\nWhy Menlo?\n\nAt Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: Proactive Leadership, Straight Talk, United Impact, Elevated Talent, and Customer-Compelled. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.\n\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability.\n\nTO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"10af591c-f29c-4e04-985f-7dacabcb26a3","title":"Sales Engineer","department":"Sales","team":"Sales","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"APAC - India","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-10T16:18:51.837+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Karnataka","addressCountry":"India","addressLocality":"Bangalore"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/10af591c-f29c-4e04-985f-7dacabcb26a3","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/10af591c-f29c-4e04-985f-7dacabcb26a3/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.</p><h2><strong>Summary</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Menlo Security Sales Engineer is a customer-focused, technical sales professional who provides guidance and support to prospective and current customers across the region. Partnering closely with Regional Sales Managers and channel partners, the Sales Engineer scopes, recommends, and demonstrates security-focused solutions that map to each customer's business needs and budget. Acting in a consultative capacity, they serve as a trusted technical resource for account teams, partners, and customers alike. The team uses AI-assisted tools throughout the sales cycle, from account research and call preparation to drafting technical responses, so more time goes to the customer conversation and less to administration.</p><h2><strong>Outcomes &amp; KPIs</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Outcome(s) Owned:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Technical wins on regional sales opportunities, from discovery through successful proof of concept to close.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner technical self-sufficiency across the assigned region.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Success Metrics / KPIs:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Technical win rate on supported opportunities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proof of concept conversion rate (POC to closed-won)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Average POC cycle time from kickoff to technical decision</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Number of partner engineers enabled/certified per quarter</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Quality of field feedback delivered to Product Management and Engineering (adoption of submitted insights)</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Articulate the benefits of Menlo Security solutions to both technical and non-technical audiences, and research the technical requirements of each opportunity to scope and architect a solution that meets the customer's needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understand the customer's business drivers and map them to a Menlo Security solution that fits both their needs and their budget.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead proof of concept engagements on regional sales opportunities, including deployment and configuration of Menlo Security services or software, training users on the solutions, and acting as the interface between Sales and technical staff to resolve open issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use AI-assisted tools to prepare for customer engagements (account research, competitive positioning) and to draft and refine technical documentation, RFP responses, and follow-up communications, applying your own judgment for accuracy and fit.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with regional Menlo Security partners to build partner self-sufficiency and drive partner-led opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with customers to grow and expand their implementation and integration of Menlo Security products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide reporting and feedback on customer accounts and field activities to Sales, Product Management, and Engineering, using AI-generated call summaries and CRM enrichment to keep account records current with less manual effort.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Functional Competencies</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Required:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's or Master's degree in Computer Science or a related discipline, or equivalent experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Based in Singapore, with overnight travel throughout the region as needed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of pre-sales experience in the computer networking or security space</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong knowledge and hands-on experience across core areas including web proxy technologies, network security (firewalls, IDS/IPS, HTTP/SSL proxies), network engineering fundamentals (OSI model, IPv4/6, routing, switching, DNS, VLANs and subnetting), and email security and mail flow</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and oral communication skills, with the ability to articulate both the business value and the technical advantages of Menlo Security solutions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong sense of accountability and ownership, a proactive, get-it-done attitude, and a passion for continuous learning</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred / Nice to Have:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with malware analysis (static, delta, and dynamic/runtime approaches), sandboxing solutions, host-based forensics, and Windows internals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Network forensics experience, including packet capture and analysis</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Incident response experience, including workflow procedures, evidence gathering, and chain of custody handling</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enterprise architecture familiarity (Active Directory, SCCM, LDAP/RADIUS/TACACS+, two-factor authentication) and virtualization technology (VMware, Citrix, VDI)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with common hacking and exploitation tools and methodologies, malware families, and AV/IDS/IPS evasion techniques</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of Menlo Security competitors, including their solutions, strengths, and weaknesses</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency with AI-assisted sales and productivity tools (LLM-based research, drafting, and summarization) as part of your everyday workflow</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Self-directed, with the ability to prioritize and execute project tasks in a methodical, disciplined manner and set clear expectations with stakeholders and team members</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">MSGL-I4</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/\">LinkedIn</a>!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why Menlo?</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: <strong>Proactive Leadership</strong>, <strong>Straight Talk</strong>, <strong>United Impact</strong>, <strong>Elevated Talent</strong>, and <strong>Customer-Compelled</strong>. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability</strong>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>TO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.</strong></em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.\n\n\nSUMMARY\n\nThe Menlo Security Sales Engineer is a customer-focused, technical sales professional who provides guidance and support to prospective and current customers across the region. Partnering closely with Regional Sales Managers and channel partners, the Sales Engineer scopes, recommends, and demonstrates security-focused solutions that map to each customer's business needs and budget. Acting in a consultative capacity, they serve as a trusted technical resource for account teams, partners, and customers alike. The team uses AI-assisted tools throughout the sales cycle, from account research and call preparation to drafting technical responses, so more time goes to the customer conversation and less to administration.\n\n\nOUTCOMES & KPIS\n\nKey Outcome(s) Owned:\n\n - Technical wins on regional sales opportunities, from discovery through successful proof of concept to close.\n\n - Partner technical self-sufficiency across the assigned region.\n\nSuccess Metrics / KPIs:\n\n - Technical win rate on supported opportunities\n\n - Proof of concept conversion rate (POC to closed-won)\n\n - Average POC cycle time from kickoff to technical decision\n\n - Number of partner engineers enabled/certified per quarter\n\n - Quality of field feedback delivered to Product Management and Engineering (adoption of submitted insights)\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Articulate the benefits of Menlo Security solutions to both technical and non-technical audiences, and research the technical requirements of each opportunity to scope and architect a solution that meets the customer's needs.\n\n - Understand the customer's business drivers and map them to a Menlo Security solution that fits both their needs and their budget.\n\n - Lead proof of concept engagements on regional sales opportunities, including deployment and configuration of Menlo Security services or software, training users on the solutions, and acting as the interface between Sales and technical staff to resolve open issues.\n\n - Use AI-assisted tools to prepare for customer engagements (account research, competitive positioning) and to draft and refine technical documentation, RFP responses, and follow-up communications, applying your own judgment for accuracy and fit.\n\n - Work closely with regional Menlo Security partners to build partner self-sufficiency and drive partner-led opportunities.\n\n - Work closely with customers to grow and expand their implementation and integration of Menlo Security products.\n\n - Provide reporting and feedback on customer accounts and field activities to Sales, Product Management, and Engineering, using AI-generated call summaries and CRM enrichment to keep account records current with less manual effort.\n\n\nFUNCTIONAL COMPETENCIES\n\nRequired:\n\n - Bachelor's or Master's degree in Computer Science or a related discipline, or equivalent experience\n\n - Based in Singapore, with overnight travel throughout the region as needed\n\n - 4+ years of pre-sales experience in the computer networking or security space\n\n - Strong knowledge and hands-on experience across core areas including web proxy technologies, network security (firewalls, IDS/IPS, HTTP/SSL proxies), network engineering fundamentals (OSI model, IPv4/6, routing, switching, DNS, VLANs and subnetting), and email security and mail flow\n\n - Excellent written and oral communication skills, with the ability to articulate both the business value and the technical advantages of Menlo Security solutions\n\n - A strong sense of accountability and ownership, a proactive, get-it-done attitude, and a passion for continuous learning\n\nPreferred / Nice to Have:\n\n - Experience with malware analysis (static, delta, and dynamic/runtime approaches), sandboxing solutions, host-based forensics, and Windows internals\n\n - Network forensics experience, including packet capture and analysis\n\n - Incident response experience, including workflow procedures, evidence gathering, and chain of custody handling\n\n - Enterprise architecture familiarity (Active Directory, SCCM, LDAP/RADIUS/TACACS+, two-factor authentication) and virtualization technology (VMware, Citrix, VDI)\n\n - Familiarity with common hacking and exploitation tools and methodologies, malware families, and AV/IDS/IPS evasion techniques\n\n - Working knowledge of Menlo Security competitors, including their solutions, strengths, and weaknesses\n\n - Fluency with AI-assisted sales and productivity tools (LLM-based research, drafting, and summarization) as part of your everyday workflow\n\n - Self-directed, with the ability to prioritize and execute project tasks in a methodical, disciplined manner and set clear expectations with stakeholders and team members\n\n\n\nMSGL-I4\n\nFollow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/!\n\nWhy Menlo?\n\nAt Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: Proactive Leadership, Straight Talk, United Impact, Elevated Talent, and Customer-Compelled. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.\n\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability.\n\nTO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"2f364a45-2fbc-4284-836c-94b587caed61","title":"Manager,Engineering","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"APAC - India","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2025-12-17T13:14:32.638+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Karnataka","addressCountry":"India","addressLocality":"Bangalore"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/2f364a45-2fbc-4284-836c-94b587caed61","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/2f364a45-2fbc-4284-836c-94b587caed61/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About the Role</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security is looking for a talented Engineering Manager to join our team in Bangalore. You will manage employees located in Bangalore and will contribute technical leadership to the team that designs, builds, and supports the scalable, high-performance services underpinning our world-class Secure Application Access technology.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo serves millions of users on our worldwide cloud on desktop and mobile platforms. We're looking for a strong leader to guide and mentor the team in the architecture, design, development, deployment, and monitoring of our core <strong>microservices, data stores, and cloud infrastructure</strong> that power our platform.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The management team is highly experienced and collegial, with a strong design and code review culture. We encourage candidates with a background in <strong>highly scalable distributed systems, networking, and cybersecurity</strong> to apply if you feel your skill set can be applied to new challenges.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The position is full-time and based in our <strong>Bangalore, India office</strong>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Your Experience</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Requirements for the role include:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Deep expertise in one or more core backend languages</strong>, specifically <strong>Golang and/or NodeJS</strong>.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with <strong>Python </strong>is a plus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven experience in designing and building <strong>scalable, resilient microservices architectures</strong>.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong knowledge of <strong>NoSQL database technologies</strong> and experience with services like <strong>Spanner, DynamoDB, or GKE exposure</strong> for data persistence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with modern DevOps practices, including <strong>CI/CD, Terraform, Kubernetes, and Docker</strong>.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with major cloud providers, specifically <strong>GCP or AWS</strong>.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong background in <strong>Networking</strong> concepts (e.g., TCP/IP, HTTP) and <strong>Cybersecurity</strong> is a significant advantage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven experience leading and mentoring high-performing software development teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Agile development methodologies (e.g., Scrum, Kanban).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills, especially in diagnosing complex distributed system issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to provide technical guidance, perform code reviews, and debug complex, high-traffic services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written and verbal communication skills to effectively collaborate with technical and non-technical stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactive, ambitious, with a strong ability to learn new technologies and evolve team practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Highly organized and detail oriented.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>2+ years of experience</strong> in leading and building high-performing engineering teams, attracting top talent with diverse skills, and hands-on management (including responsibilities such as performance reviews, talent assessment, onboarding and training new team members, etc.)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>BE/BTech or Masters in Computer</strong> Science with 8 - 12 years of hands on Software development experience</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">MSGL-I4</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/\">LinkedIn</a>!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why Menlo?</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: <strong>Proactive Leadership</strong>, <strong>Straight Talk</strong>, <strong>United Impact</strong>, <strong>Elevated Talent</strong>, and <strong>Customer-Compelled</strong>. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability</strong>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>TO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.</strong></em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.\n\nAbout the Role\n\nMenlo Security is looking for a talented Engineering Manager to join our team in Bangalore. You will manage employees located in Bangalore and will contribute technical leadership to the team that designs, builds, and supports the scalable, high-performance services underpinning our world-class Secure Application Access technology.\n\nMenlo serves millions of users on our worldwide cloud on desktop and mobile platforms. We're looking for a strong leader to guide and mentor the team in the architecture, design, development, deployment, and monitoring of our core microservices, data stores, and cloud infrastructure that power our platform.\n\nThe management team is highly experienced and collegial, with a strong design and code review culture. We encourage candidates with a background in highly scalable distributed systems, networking, and cybersecurity to apply if you feel your skill set can be applied to new challenges.\n\nThe position is full-time and based in our Bangalore, India office.\n\n\n\n\n\nYour Experience\n\nRequirements for the role include:\n\n - Deep expertise in one or more core backend languages, specifically Golang and/or NodeJS.\n\n - Experience with Python is a plus.\n\n - Proven experience in designing and building scalable, resilient microservices architectures.\n\n - Strong knowledge of NoSQL database technologies and experience with services like Spanner, DynamoDB, or GKE exposure for data persistence.\n\n - Hands-on experience with modern DevOps practices, including CI/CD, Terraform, Kubernetes, and Docker.\n\n - Experience with major cloud providers, specifically GCP or AWS.\n\n - A strong background in Networking concepts (e.g., TCP/IP, HTTP) and Cybersecurity is a significant advantage.\n\n - Proven experience leading and mentoring high-performing software development teams.\n\n - Experience with Agile development methodologies (e.g., Scrum, Kanban).\n\n - Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills, especially in diagnosing complex distributed system issues.\n\n - Ability to provide technical guidance, perform code reviews, and debug complex, high-traffic services.\n\n - Strong written and verbal communication skills to effectively collaborate with technical and non-technical stakeholders.\n\n - Proactive, ambitious, with a strong ability to learn new technologies and evolve team practices.\n\n - Highly organized and detail oriented.\n\n - 2+ years of experience in leading and building high-performing engineering teams, attracting top talent with diverse skills, and hands-on management (including responsibilities such as performance reviews, talent assessment, onboarding and training new team members, etc.)\n\nBE/BTech or Masters in Computer Science with 8 - 12 years of hands on Software development experience\n\n\n\nMSGL-I4\n\nFollow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/!\n\nWhy Menlo?\n\nAt Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: Proactive Leadership, Straight Talk, United Impact, Elevated Talent, and Customer-Compelled. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.\n\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability.\n\nTO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"36fd13f6-aa69-40ad-b06c-5dd6301bebb1","title":"Senior Security Engineer - Pentester","department":"CISO-R&D","team":"CISO-R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"AMER - Canada","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-03T17:45:57.176+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Canada"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/36fd13f6-aa69-40ad-b06c-5dd6301bebb1","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/36fd13f6-aa69-40ad-b06c-5dd6301bebb1/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.</p><h2><strong>Summary</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a forward-thinking Security Engineer to join our security team, focused on offensive and defensive testing, penetration testing of product features, and the cloud architecture behind the product. You'll operate across a complex multi-cloud environment (AWS &amp; GCP) spanning traditional VMs and modern managed and unmanaged container-based architectures, partnering with fellow Penetration Testing and Cloud Security engineers to run targeted assessments during the testing window immediately before each release. The role reaches beyond the application layer into the Control Plane, reviewing cloud configurations, IAM policies, and orchestration layers against security baselines, and extends to the frontline of external defense by triaging bug bounty submissions and outside vulnerability reports. AI and large language models are core to how this team works day to day — you'll use them to accelerate reconnaissance, generate attack vectors, analyze configurations, and draft vulnerability reports, while applying human judgment to validate findings and communicate risk clearly to product teams. Speed matters here: the team's operating cadence is built around identifying, validating, and reporting vulnerabilities quickly enough to keep pace with release velocity.<br /></p><h2><strong>Outcomes &amp; KPIs</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Outcome(s) Owned:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure new product features and the underlying multi-cloud (AWS/GCP) infrastructure are rigorously security-tested before release, and that vulnerabilities surfaced internally or via bug bounty are triaged and communicated with speed and precision.<br /></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Success Metrics / KPIs</strong>:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Percentage of roadmap features assessed within the pre-release testing window.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mean time to triage and validate bug bounty / external vulnerability reports.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reduction in critical/high-severity vulnerabilities escaping to production post-release.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Time saved per assessment cycle through AI-assisted tooling and automation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Quality and actionability of vulnerability reports and PoCs, as rated by product teams.<br /></p></li></ul><h2><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct deep-dive penetration tests of products across a multi-cloud (AWS &amp; GCP) environment, working in tandem with a peer pentester.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review IAM policies, service configurations, and cloud-native permission structures across the Control Plane to ensure cloud configurations meet security baselines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Execute dynamic testing against web interfaces and API endpoints (Data Plane &amp; Web UI).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assess the security posture of hybrid infrastructure spanning containers and virtual machines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Triage findings, build clear and reproducible proofs-of-concept, and partner with product teams to explain risk and drive remediation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use AI and large language models to automate reconnaissance, generate attack vectors, analyze configurations, and draft vulnerability reports, applying strong prompt-engineering skills to security contexts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor bug bounty pipelines and external reports, validating findings and managing researcher communication.<br /></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Functional Competencies</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Required:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Multi-Cloud Fluency:</strong> Deep architectural understanding of GCP and AWS. Capable of pivoting seamlessly between providers, performing manual configuration reviews of complex IAM/Resource hierarchies, and leveraging native APIs or modern CSPM frameworks to validate security controls.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Container Security:</strong> Proven experience auditing and hardening managed container services (GKE Autopilot/Standard, EKS, ECS) and self-hosted/unmanaged workloads (K8s, k3s, OCI-runc).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>AI Tooling:</strong> Demonstrated ability to integrate AI/LLM tools (e.g., Gemini, Claude) into the pentesting lifecycle to increase speed and coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Web Application Security:</strong> Expert-level knowledge of web application security principles and offensive testing methodologies, with deep proficiency in OWASP Top 10 vulnerabilities, modern web framework exploitation, and API security (REST, WebSockets). Extensive hands-on experience conducting manual security assessments using Burp Suite Professional, OWASP ZAP, or similar tooling. Strong understanding of browser security mechanisms (CSP, CORS, SameSite cookies, Subresource Integrity), secure authentication/authorization patterns (OAuth 2.0, OIDC, JWT), and security header configurations (HSTS, X-Frame-Options, Permissions-Policy). Proven ability to identify complex security flaws beyond automated scanner detection, validate findings through proof-of-concept development, and provide actionable remediation guidance to engineering teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Security Automation:</strong> Proficiency in Python, Go, or Bash to eliminate \"toil\" — writing custom scripts and tooling to automate vulnerability discovery, validate security controls, and streamline testing workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Infrastructure as Code:</strong> Solid grasp of Terraform and cloud-native deployment patterns; able to interpret and audit complex HCL files to identify misconfigurations before they are provisioned.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Communication:</strong> Ability to write high-quality technical reports that Product Teams can easily understand and act upon.<br /></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred / Nice to Have:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Gatekeeper policies and Binary Authorization.<br /></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Our Compensation and Benefits</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Menlo Security, Base Salary is one part of our competitive total compensation and benefits package and is determined using a salary range. The base salary range for this role is 158,000 CAD - 237,000 CAD.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In accordance with Canadian law, the range provided is Menlo Security’s reasonable estimate of the base compensation for this role. The actual amount may be higher or lower, based on non-discriminatory factors such as experience, knowledge, skills, abilities, and location. All employees may be eligible to become Menlo Security shareholders through eligibility for stock-based compensation grants, which are awarded to employees based on company and individual performance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security does not accept unsolicited resumes from search firm recruiters. Fees will not be paid in the event a candidate submitted by a recruiter without an agreement in place is hired; such resumes will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security is an equal opportunity employer. All aspects of employment will be based on merit, competence, performance, and business needs. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, marital status, age, national origin, ancestry, physical or mental disability, medical condition, pregnancy, genetic information, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, veteran status, or any other status protected under federal, state, or local law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">MSGL-I4</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/\">LinkedIn</a>!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why Menlo?</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: <strong>Proactive Leadership</strong>, <strong>Straight Talk</strong>, <strong>United Impact</strong>, <strong>Elevated Talent</strong>, and <strong>Customer-Compelled</strong>. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability</strong>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>TO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.</strong></em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.\n\n\nSUMMARY\n\nWe're looking for a forward-thinking Security Engineer to join our security team, focused on offensive and defensive testing, penetration testing of product features, and the cloud architecture behind the product. You'll operate across a complex multi-cloud environment (AWS & GCP) spanning traditional VMs and modern managed and unmanaged container-based architectures, partnering with fellow Penetration Testing and Cloud Security engineers to run targeted assessments during the testing window immediately before each release. The role reaches beyond the application layer into the Control Plane, reviewing cloud configurations, IAM policies, and orchestration layers against security baselines, and extends to the frontline of external defense by triaging bug bounty submissions and outside vulnerability reports. AI and large language models are core to how this team works day to day — you'll use them to accelerate reconnaissance, generate attack vectors, analyze configurations, and draft vulnerability reports, while applying human judgment to validate findings and communicate risk clearly to product teams. Speed matters here: the team's operating cadence is built around identifying, validating, and reporting vulnerabilities quickly enough to keep pace with release velocity.\n\n\n\nOUTCOMES & KPIS\n\nKey Outcome(s) Owned:\n\n - Ensure new product features and the underlying multi-cloud (AWS/GCP) infrastructure are rigorously security-tested before release, and that vulnerabilities surfaced internally or via bug bounty are triaged and communicated with speed and precision.\n   \n\nSuccess Metrics / KPIs:\n\n - Percentage of roadmap features assessed within the pre-release testing window.\n\n - Mean time to triage and validate bug bounty / external vulnerability reports.\n\n - Reduction in critical/high-severity vulnerabilities escaping to production post-release.\n\n - Time saved per assessment cycle through AI-assisted tooling and automation.\n\n - Quality and actionability of vulnerability reports and PoCs, as rated by product teams.\n   \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Conduct deep-dive penetration tests of products across a multi-cloud (AWS & GCP) environment, working in tandem with a peer pentester.\n\n - Review IAM policies, service configurations, and cloud-native permission structures across the Control Plane to ensure cloud configurations meet security baselines.\n\n - Execute dynamic testing against web interfaces and API endpoints (Data Plane & Web UI).\n\n - Assess the security posture of hybrid infrastructure spanning containers and virtual machines.\n\n - Triage findings, build clear and reproducible proofs-of-concept, and partner with product teams to explain risk and drive remediation.\n\n - Use AI and large language models to automate reconnaissance, generate attack vectors, analyze configurations, and draft vulnerability reports, applying strong prompt-engineering skills to security contexts.\n\n - Monitor bug bounty pipelines and external reports, validating findings and managing researcher communication.\n   \n\n\nFUNCTIONAL COMPETENCIES\n\nRequired:\n\n - Multi-Cloud Fluency: Deep architectural understanding of GCP and AWS. Capable of pivoting seamlessly between providers, performing manual configuration reviews of complex IAM/Resource hierarchies, and leveraging native APIs or modern CSPM frameworks to validate security controls.\n\n - Container Security: Proven experience auditing and hardening managed container services (GKE Autopilot/Standard, EKS, ECS) and self-hosted/unmanaged workloads (K8s, k3s, OCI-runc).\n\n - AI Tooling: Demonstrated ability to integrate AI/LLM tools (e.g., Gemini, Claude) into the pentesting lifecycle to increase speed and coverage.\n\n - Web Application Security: Expert-level knowledge of web application security principles and offensive testing methodologies, with deep proficiency in OWASP Top 10 vulnerabilities, modern web framework exploitation, and API security (REST, WebSockets). Extensive hands-on experience conducting manual security assessments using Burp Suite Professional, OWASP ZAP, or similar tooling. Strong understanding of browser security mechanisms (CSP, CORS, SameSite cookies, Subresource Integrity), secure authentication/authorization patterns (OAuth 2.0, OIDC, JWT), and security header configurations (HSTS, X-Frame-Options, Permissions-Policy). Proven ability to identify complex security flaws beyond automated scanner detection, validate findings through proof-of-concept development, and provide actionable remediation guidance to engineering teams.\n\n - Security Automation: Proficiency in Python, Go, or Bash to eliminate \"toil\" — writing custom scripts and tooling to automate vulnerability discovery, validate security controls, and streamline testing workflows.\n\n - Infrastructure as Code: Solid grasp of Terraform and cloud-native deployment patterns; able to interpret and audit complex HCL files to identify misconfigurations before they are provisioned.\n\n - Communication: Ability to write high-quality technical reports that Product Teams can easily understand and act upon.\n   \n\nPreferred / Nice to Have:\n\n - Experience with Gatekeeper policies and Binary Authorization.\n   \n\nOur Compensation and Benefits\n\nAt Menlo Security, Base Salary is one part of our competitive total compensation and benefits package and is determined using a salary range. The base salary range for this role is 158,000 CAD - 237,000 CAD.\n\nIn accordance with Canadian law, the range provided is Menlo Security’s reasonable estimate of the base compensation for this role. The actual amount may be higher or lower, based on non-discriminatory factors such as experience, knowledge, skills, abilities, and location. All employees may be eligible to become Menlo Security shareholders through eligibility for stock-based compensation grants, which are awarded to employees based on company and individual performance.\n\nMenlo Security does not accept unsolicited resumes from search firm recruiters. Fees will not be paid in the event a candidate submitted by a recruiter without an agreement in place is hired; such resumes will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. \n\nMenlo Security is an equal opportunity employer. All aspects of employment will be based on merit, competence, performance, and business needs. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, marital status, age, national origin, ancestry, physical or mental disability, medical condition, pregnancy, genetic information, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, veteran status, or any other status protected under federal, state, or local law.\n\n \n\nMSGL-I4\n\nFollow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/!\n\nWhy Menlo?\n\nAt Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: Proactive Leadership, Straight Talk, United Impact, Elevated Talent, and Customer-Compelled. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.\n\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability.\n\nTO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"f6e658d0-1388-463b-8109-2716a64335a3","title":"Senior Engineer I(UK region)","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"EMEA - UK","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-04-15T08:46:07.394+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Berkshire","addressCountry":"United Kingdom","addressLocality":"Bracknell"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/f6e658d0-1388-463b-8109-2716a64335a3","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/f6e658d0-1388-463b-8109-2716a64335a3/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About the role</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security is looking for talented engineers to join our US/UK Web Isolation team. You will be responsible for extending and supporting our world-class remote browser technology on desktop and mobile platforms, serving millions of users on Menlo’s worldwide cloud. Example work areas include Chromium internals, networking, video/audio, advanced HTML5 features, containerization, load balancing, scaling and cost-saving; all of it with a strong security focus. The Web Isolation team is highly experienced and collegial, with a strong design and code review culture. We encourage candidates with deep systems-level experience in non-browser technology areas to apply if you feel your skill set can be applied to new challenges. The blog posting<u> </u><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.menlosecurity.com/blog/the-mobile-isolation-era-begins\"><u>https://www.menlosecurity.com/blog/the-mobile-isolation-era-begins</u></a> gives an introduction to some of those challenges.<br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Your Experience</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ideal candidate already understands browsers at a deep level. You have (or will gain) rich experience in Chromium internals, networking, video/audio, and advanced HTML5 features such as WebGL and WebRTC.<br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Requirements for the role include:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">● Excellent C++ skills.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">● Ability to use modern AI tooling in development workflows</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">● Strong knowledge of Python, Rust and Javascript are highly desirable </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">● Strong networking fundamentals</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">● Strong knowledge of HTTP security is highly desirable</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">● Experience implementing and maintaining features in Chromium or other browser platforms at various layers, including content, browser, core, compositor, skia and networking</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">● Systems-level Linux experience</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">● Good to have: Tornado, haproxy, AWS EC2, WebGL, WebRTC, font rendering, input experience including IME and contenteditable</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">● Ability to write clean, concise and maintainable code</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">● Strong written and verbal communication skills</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">● Proactive, ambitious, and strong ability to learn new things</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">● Highly organized and detailed with critical attention to detail and documentation </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">● BSc or higher degree in Computer Science or related field.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">MSGL-I4</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/\">LinkedIn</a>!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why Menlo?</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: <strong>Proactive Leadership</strong>, <strong>Straight Talk</strong>, <strong>United Impact</strong>, <strong>Elevated Talent</strong>, and <strong>Customer-Compelled</strong>. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability</strong>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>TO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.</strong></em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.\n\nAbout the role\n\nMenlo Security is looking for talented engineers to join our US/UK Web Isolation team. You will be responsible for extending and supporting our world-class remote browser technology on desktop and mobile platforms, serving millions of users on Menlo’s worldwide cloud. Example work areas include Chromium internals, networking, video/audio, advanced HTML5 features, containerization, load balancing, scaling and cost-saving; all of it with a strong security focus. The Web Isolation team is highly experienced and collegial, with a strong design and code review culture. We encourage candidates with deep systems-level experience in non-browser technology areas to apply if you feel your skill set can be applied to new challenges. The blog posting https://www.menlosecurity.com/blog/the-mobile-isolation-era-begins gives an introduction to some of those challenges.\n\n\nYour Experience\n\nThe ideal candidate already understands browsers at a deep level. You have (or will gain) rich experience in Chromium internals, networking, video/audio, and advanced HTML5 features such as WebGL and WebRTC.\n\n\nRequirements for the role include:\n\n● Excellent C++ skills.\n\n● Ability to use modern AI tooling in development workflows\n\n● Strong knowledge of Python, Rust and Javascript are highly desirable \n\n● Strong networking fundamentals\n\n● Strong knowledge of HTTP security is highly desirable\n\n● Experience implementing and maintaining features in Chromium or other browser platforms at various layers, including content, browser, core, compositor, skia and networking\n\n● Systems-level Linux experience\n\n● Good to have: Tornado, haproxy, AWS EC2, WebGL, WebRTC, font rendering, input experience including IME and contenteditable\n\n● Ability to write clean, concise and maintainable code\n\n● Strong written and verbal communication skills\n\n● Proactive, ambitious, and strong ability to learn new things\n\n● Highly organized and detailed with critical attention to detail and documentation \n\n● BSc or higher degree in Computer Science or related field.\n\n\n\nMSGL-I4\n\nFollow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/!\n\nWhy Menlo?\n\nAt Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: Proactive Leadership, Straight Talk, United Impact, Elevated Talent, and Customer-Compelled. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.\n\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability.\n\nTO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"e41e7613-f4a0-40f6-8aea-f895af9f021f","title":"Principal Platform Infrastructure Engineer (SRE Enablement)","department":"Infrastructure","team":"Infrastructure","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"EMEA - Distributed (UK)","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-12T14:59:14.848+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United Kingdom","addressLocality":""}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/e41e7613-f4a0-40f6-8aea-f895af9f021f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/e41e7613-f4a0-40f6-8aea-f895af9f021f/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.</p><h2>About the Role</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Platform Infrastructure Engineering is responsible for building and operating Menlo Security's Infrastructure Platform. Together with the rest of our engineering teams, we enable our customers to connect to the Internet without compromise. Our environment provides services globally. We expect failure, build security in by design, create evolvable systems, and enable multi-tenancy across the infrastructure. Automation is an absolute for us.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to getting it done properly, the first time.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Platform Infrastructure Engineer, you'll join a group of experienced engineers who are part of a globally distributed team responsible for building and managing the company's core infrastructure services and maintaining our constantly growing platform. The team operates a sophisticated cloud-native infrastructure built on Google Kubernetes Engine and VMs spanning multiple environments globally from development to production. We manage infrastructure as code with Terraform and Spacelift orchestration, and deploy services using Helm charts. Our platform emphasizes security-first design, comprehensive observability, and multi-region resilience. Success in this role requires working with a vast VM fleet in AWS and GCP as well as Kubernetes, writing Infrastructure as Code, and a passion for automation and reliability engineering.</p><h2>Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Architect and govern the design, deployment, and operation of high-scale, multi-region VM and Kubernetes infrastructure on GCP and AWS, ensuring maximum resilience and performance across all environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive cross-functional technical alignment with Engineering, Product, Compliance, and Security teams, serving as the architectural consultant and leader for major initiatives involving capacity planning, disaster recovery, and cloud-native application design.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define and enforce organizational best practices and standards for Infrastructure as Code (IaC) using Terraform and Spacelift, ensuring consistency and security across all provisioned cloud resources (GCP/AWS).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and manage complex, multi-layer configuration management and deployment workflows that optimize reliability and operational efficiency across the entire platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set the technical direction and implement comprehensive observability solutions (Grafana Cloud, Prometheus/Mimir, OTel collectors), establishing organization-wide standards for system visibility, metrics, and alerting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define the strategic architecture and lifecycle management of core platform services, including certificate management, DNS automation, ingress controllers, and service mesh networking (Cilium).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactively identify and lead large-scale strategic efforts to eliminate technical toil and improve operational efficiency through the development of tools, strategic automation, and building advanced CI/CD pipelines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentor and provide deep technical guidance to both junior and senior engineers within Platform Infrastructure Engineering.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in a 24x7 on-call rotation as part of a globally distributed team, responding to incidents and driving post-incident reviews to ensure long-term solutions and process i</p></li></ul><h2>Requirements</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, similar technical field of study, or equivalent practical experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in common programming &amp; scripting languages. We use a lot of python, bash and go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of network topologies, communication protocols (ie. TCP/IP, HTTP/S, UDP, TLS)  and enterprise grade connectivity solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Kubernetes expertise including cluster administration, RBAC, networking, workload management, and troubleshooting across production environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven experience with Terraform for infrastructure provisioning and management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of Google Cloud Platform services including GKE, VPC networking, Cloud DNS, Artifact Registry, Secret Manager, IAM, Gemini Code Assist, and Workload Identity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience and success mentoring other junior and senior engineers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with GitOps methodologies and tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear understanding of how to use LLM code assist tools to effectively build software.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/\">LinkedIn</a>!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why Menlo?</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: <strong>Proactive Leadership</strong>, <strong>Straight Talk</strong>, <strong>United Impact</strong>, <strong>Elevated Talent</strong>, and <strong>Customer-Compelled</strong>. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability</strong>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>TO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.</strong></em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nPlatform Infrastructure Engineering is responsible for building and operating Menlo Security's Infrastructure Platform. Together with the rest of our engineering teams, we enable our customers to connect to the Internet without compromise. Our environment provides services globally. We expect failure, build security in by design, create evolvable systems, and enable multi-tenancy across the infrastructure. Automation is an absolute for us.\n\n\n\nWe are committed to getting it done properly, the first time.\n\n\n\nAs a Platform Infrastructure Engineer, you'll join a group of experienced engineers who are part of a globally distributed team responsible for building and managing the company's core infrastructure services and maintaining our constantly growing platform. The team operates a sophisticated cloud-native infrastructure built on Google Kubernetes Engine and VMs spanning multiple environments globally from development to production. We manage infrastructure as code with Terraform and Spacelift orchestration, and deploy services using Helm charts. Our platform emphasizes security-first design, comprehensive observability, and multi-region resilience. Success in this role requires working with a vast VM fleet in AWS and GCP as well as Kubernetes, writing Infrastructure as Code, and a passion for automation and reliability engineering.\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Architect and govern the design, deployment, and operation of high-scale, multi-region VM and Kubernetes infrastructure on GCP and AWS, ensuring maximum resilience and performance across all environments.\n\n - Drive cross-functional technical alignment with Engineering, Product, Compliance, and Security teams, serving as the architectural consultant and leader for major initiatives involving capacity planning, disaster recovery, and cloud-native application design.\n\n - Define and enforce organizational best practices and standards for Infrastructure as Code (IaC) using Terraform and Spacelift, ensuring consistency and security across all provisioned cloud resources (GCP/AWS).\n\n - Design and manage complex, multi-layer configuration management and deployment workflows that optimize reliability and operational efficiency across the entire platform.\n\n - Set the technical direction and implement comprehensive observability solutions (Grafana Cloud, Prometheus/Mimir, OTel collectors), establishing organization-wide standards for system visibility, metrics, and alerting.\n\n - Define the strategic architecture and lifecycle management of core platform services, including certificate management, DNS automation, ingress controllers, and service mesh networking (Cilium).\n\n - Proactively identify and lead large-scale strategic efforts to eliminate technical toil and improve operational efficiency through the development of tools, strategic automation, and building advanced CI/CD pipelines.\n\n - Mentor and provide deep technical guidance to both junior and senior engineers within Platform Infrastructure Engineering.\n\n - Participate in a 24x7 on-call rotation as part of a globally distributed team, responding to incidents and driving post-incident reviews to ensure long-term solutions and process i\n\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n\n - Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, similar technical field of study, or equivalent practical experience.\n\n - Proficiency in common programming & scripting languages. We use a lot of python, bash and go.\n\n - Understanding of network topologies, communication protocols (ie. TCP/IP, HTTP/S, UDP, TLS)  and enterprise grade connectivity solutions.\n\n - Kubernetes expertise including cluster administration, RBAC, networking, workload management, and troubleshooting across production environments.\n\n - Proven experience with Terraform for infrastructure provisioning and management.\n\n - Knowledge of Google Cloud Platform services including GKE, VPC networking, Cloud DNS, Artifact Registry, Secret Manager, IAM, Gemini Code Assist, and Workload Identity.\n\n - Prior experience and success mentoring other junior and senior engineers\n\n - Experience with GitOps methodologies and tools.\n\n - Clear understanding of how to use LLM code assist tools to effectively build software.\n\nFollow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/!\n\nWhy Menlo?\n\nAt Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: Proactive Leadership, Straight Talk, United Impact, Elevated Talent, and Customer-Compelled. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.\n\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability.\n\nTO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"dd0e16f2-893e-43d1-a1e4-15f080a4f8ae","title":"Principal Platform Infrastructure Engineer (Containers)","department":"Infrastructure","team":"Infrastructure","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"AMER - Canada","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-04T16:31:47.779+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Canada"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/dd0e16f2-893e-43d1-a1e4-15f080a4f8ae","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/dd0e16f2-893e-43d1-a1e4-15f080a4f8ae/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About the Role</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Platform Infrastructure Engineering is responsible for building and operating Menlo Security's Infrastructure Platform. Together with the rest of our engineering teams, we enable our customers to connect to the Internet without compromise. Our environment provides services globally. We expect failure, build security in by design, create evolvable systems, and enable multi-tenancy across the infrastructure. Automation is an absolute for us.<br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to getting it done properly, the first time.<br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Platform Infrastructure Engineer, you'll join a group of experienced engineers who are part of a globally distributed team responsible for building and managing the company's core infrastructure services and maintaining our constantly growing platform. The team operates a sophisticated cloud-native infrastructure built on Google Kubernetes Engine and VMs spanning multiple environments globally from development to production. We manage infrastructure as code with Terraform and Spacelift orchestration, and deploy services using Helm charts. Our platform emphasizes security-first design, comprehensive observability, and multi-region resilience. Success in this role requires working with a vast VM fleet in AWS and GCP as well as Kubernetes, writing Infrastructure as Code, and a passion for automation and reliability engineering.<br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, deploy, and maintain VM and Kubernetes infrastructure on GCP and AWS across dozens of clusters spanning development, staging, and production environments in multiple regions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate with your peers in your direct team as well as across teams to ensure that the tasks you’re working on are going to solve the problems that we need them to solve. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain Infrastructure as Code (IaC) using Terraform modules, managing resources through Spacelift or equivalent Terraform Automation and Collaboration Software (TACOS). Provision cloud infrastructure including networking, compute, storage, and security components primarily on GCP, with secondary AWS support. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Implement and manage workflows with sophisticated multi-layer configuration management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain comprehensive observability solutions using Grafana Cloud, Prometheus/Mimir, and OTel collectors. Design Grafana dashboards, configure alerting rules, and ensure visibility across all platform components.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage certificate lifecycle, DNS automation, ingress controllers, and service mesh networking with Cilium.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Engineering, Product, Compliance, and Security teams to design resilient, scalable systems. Consult on capacity planning, disaster recovery, and architectural decisions for cloud-native applications.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and eliminate toil through automation. Write scripts, develop tools, and build CI/CD pipelines to improve operational efficiency and reduce manual work. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in a 24x7 on-call rotation as part of a globally distributed team, responding to incidents and driving post-incident reviews.<br /></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, similar technical field of study, or equivalent practical experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in common programming &amp; scripting languages. We use a lot of python, bash and go.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of network topologies, communication protocols (ie. TCP/IP, HTTP/S, UDP, TLS) and enterprise grade connectivity solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Kubernetes expertise including cluster administration, RBAC, networking, workload management, and troubleshooting across production environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven experience with Terraform for infrastructure provisioning and management. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of Google Cloud Platform services including GKE, VPC networking, Cloud DNS, Artifact Registry, Secret Manager, IAM, Gemini Code Assist, and Workload Identity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with GitOps methodologies and tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear understanding of how to use LLM code assist tools to effectively build software.<br /></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Our Compensation and Benefits</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Menlo Security, Base Salary is one part of our competitive total compensation and benefits package and is determined using a salary range. The base salary range for this role is 141,000 CAD - 249,000 CAD.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In accordance with Canadian law, the range provided is Menlo Security’s reasonable estimate of the base compensation for this role. The actual amount may be higher or lower, based on non-discriminatory factors such as experience, knowledge, skills, abilities, and location. All employees may be eligible to become Menlo Security shareholders through eligibility for stock-based compensation grants, which are awarded to employees based on company and individual performance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security does not accept unsolicited resumes from search firm recruiters. Fees will not be paid in the event a candidate submitted by a recruiter without an agreement in place is hired; such resumes will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security is an equal opportunity employer. All aspects of employment will be based on merit, competence, performance, and business needs. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, marital status, age, national origin, ancestry, physical or mental disability, medical condition, pregnancy, genetic information, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, veteran status, or any other status protected under federal, state, or local law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">MSGL-I4</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/\">LinkedIn</a>!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why Menlo?</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: <strong>Proactive Leadership</strong>, <strong>Straight Talk</strong>, <strong>United Impact</strong>, <strong>Elevated Talent</strong>, and <strong>Customer-Compelled</strong>. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability</strong>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>TO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.</strong></em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.\n\nAbout the Role\n\nPlatform Infrastructure Engineering is responsible for building and operating Menlo Security's Infrastructure Platform. Together with the rest of our engineering teams, we enable our customers to connect to the Internet without compromise. Our environment provides services globally. We expect failure, build security in by design, create evolvable systems, and enable multi-tenancy across the infrastructure. Automation is an absolute for us.\n\n\nWe are committed to getting it done properly, the first time.\n\n\nAs a Platform Infrastructure Engineer, you'll join a group of experienced engineers who are part of a globally distributed team responsible for building and managing the company's core infrastructure services and maintaining our constantly growing platform. The team operates a sophisticated cloud-native infrastructure built on Google Kubernetes Engine and VMs spanning multiple environments globally from development to production. We manage infrastructure as code with Terraform and Spacelift orchestration, and deploy services using Helm charts. Our platform emphasizes security-first design, comprehensive observability, and multi-region resilience. Success in this role requires working with a vast VM fleet in AWS and GCP as well as Kubernetes, writing Infrastructure as Code, and a passion for automation and reliability engineering.\n\n\nResponsibilities\n\n - Design, deploy, and maintain VM and Kubernetes infrastructure on GCP and AWS across dozens of clusters spanning development, staging, and production environments in multiple regions.\n\n - Coordinate with your peers in your direct team as well as across teams to ensure that the tasks you’re working on are going to solve the problems that we need them to solve. \n\n - Build and maintain Infrastructure as Code (IaC) using Terraform modules, managing resources through Spacelift or equivalent Terraform Automation and Collaboration Software (TACOS). Provision cloud infrastructure including networking, compute, storage, and security components primarily on GCP, with secondary AWS support. \n\n - Implement and manage workflows with sophisticated multi-layer configuration management.\n\n - Build and maintain comprehensive observability solutions using Grafana Cloud, Prometheus/Mimir, and OTel collectors. Design Grafana dashboards, configure alerting rules, and ensure visibility across all platform components.\n\n - Manage certificate lifecycle, DNS automation, ingress controllers, and service mesh networking with Cilium.\n\n - Partner with Engineering, Product, Compliance, and Security teams to design resilient, scalable systems. Consult on capacity planning, disaster recovery, and architectural decisions for cloud-native applications.\n\n - Identify and eliminate toil through automation. Write scripts, develop tools, and build CI/CD pipelines to improve operational efficiency and reduce manual work. \n\n - Participate in a 24x7 on-call rotation as part of a globally distributed team, responding to incidents and driving post-incident reviews.\n   \n\nRequirements\n\n - Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, similar technical field of study, or equivalent practical experience.\n\n - Proficiency in common programming & scripting languages. We use a lot of python, bash and go.\n\n - Understanding of network topologies, communication protocols (ie. TCP/IP, HTTP/S, UDP, TLS) and enterprise grade connectivity solutions.\n\n - Kubernetes expertise including cluster administration, RBAC, networking, workload management, and troubleshooting across production environments.\n\n - Proven experience with Terraform for infrastructure provisioning and management. \n\n - Knowledge of Google Cloud Platform services including GKE, VPC networking, Cloud DNS, Artifact Registry, Secret Manager, IAM, Gemini Code Assist, and Workload Identity.\n\n - Experience with GitOps methodologies and tools.\n\n - Clear understanding of how to use LLM code assist tools to effectively build software.\n   \n\nOur Compensation and Benefits\n\nAt Menlo Security, Base Salary is one part of our competitive total compensation and benefits package and is determined using a salary range. The base salary range for this role is 141,000 CAD - 249,000 CAD.\n\nIn accordance with Canadian law, the range provided is Menlo Security’s reasonable estimate of the base compensation for this role. The actual amount may be higher or lower, based on non-discriminatory factors such as experience, knowledge, skills, abilities, and location. All employees may be eligible to become Menlo Security shareholders through eligibility for stock-based compensation grants, which are awarded to employees based on company and individual performance.\n\nMenlo Security does not accept unsolicited resumes from search firm recruiters. Fees will not be paid in the event a candidate submitted by a recruiter without an agreement in place is hired; such resumes will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. \n\nMenlo Security is an equal opportunity employer. All aspects of employment will be based on merit, competence, performance, and business needs. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, marital status, age, national origin, ancestry, physical or mental disability, medical condition, pregnancy, genetic information, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, veteran status, or any other status protected under federal, state, or local law.\n\n \n\nMSGL-I4\n\nFollow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/!\n\nWhy Menlo?\n\nAt Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: Proactive Leadership, Straight Talk, United Impact, Elevated Talent, and Customer-Compelled. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.\n\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability.\n\nTO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"43eeea4f-8c6e-4176-8ab4-1e03c3346e80","title":"Sales Engineer ","department":"Sales","team":"Sales Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"APAC - Singapore","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-27T13:24:57.786+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Singapore","addressCountry":"Singapore","addressLocality":"Singapore"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/43eeea4f-8c6e-4176-8ab4-1e03c3346e80","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/43eeea4f-8c6e-4176-8ab4-1e03c3346e80/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.</p><h2><strong>Summary</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Menlo Security Sales Engineer is a customer-focused, technical sales professional who provides guidance and support to prospective and current customers across the region. Partnering closely with Regional Sales Managers and channel partners, the Sales Engineer scopes, recommends, and demonstrates security-focused solutions that map to each customer's business needs and budget. Acting in a consultative capacity, they serve as a trusted technical resource for account teams, partners, and customers alike. The team uses AI-assisted tools throughout the sales cycle, from account research and call preparation to drafting technical responses, so more time goes to the customer conversation and less to administration.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Outcomes &amp; KPIs</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Outcome(s) Owned:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Technical wins on regional sales opportunities, from discovery through successful proof of concept to close.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner technical self-sufficiency across the assigned region.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Success Metrics / KPIs (drafted, for hiring manager review):</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Technical win rate on supported opportunities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proof of concept conversion rate (POC to closed-won)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Average POC cycle time from kickoff to technical decision</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Number of partner engineers enabled/certified per quarter</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Quality of field feedback delivered to Product Management and Engineering (adoption of submitted insights)</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Articulate the benefits of Menlo Security solutions to both technical and non-technical audiences, and research the technical requirements of each opportunity to scope and architect a solution that meets the customer's needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understand the customer's business drivers and map them to a Menlo Security solution that fits both their needs and their budget.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead proof of concept engagements on regional sales opportunities, including deployment and configuration of Menlo Security services or software, training users on the solutions, and acting as the interface between Sales and technical staff to resolve open issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use AI-assisted tools to prepare for customer engagements (account research, competitive positioning) and to draft and refine technical documentation, RFP responses, and follow-up communications, applying your own judgment for accuracy and fit.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with regional Menlo Security partners to build partner self-sufficiency and drive partner-led opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with customers to grow and expand their implementation and integration of Menlo Security products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide reporting and feedback on customer accounts and field activities to Sales, Product Management, and Engineering, using AI-generated call summaries and CRM enrichment to keep account records current with less manual effort.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Functional Competencies</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Required:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's or Master's degree in Computer Science or a related discipline, or equivalent experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Based in Singapore, with overnight travel throughout the region as needed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of pre-sales experience in the computer networking or security space</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong knowledge and hands-on experience across core areas including web proxy technologies, network security (firewalls, IDS/IPS, HTTP/SSL proxies), network engineering fundamentals (OSI model, IPv4/6, routing, switching, DNS, VLANs and subnetting), and email security and mail flow</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and oral communication skills, with the ability to articulate both the business value and the technical advantages of Menlo Security solutions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong sense of accountability and ownership, a proactive, get-it-done attitude, and a passion for continuous learning</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred / Nice to Have:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with malware analysis (static, delta, and dynamic/runtime approaches), sandboxing solutions, host-based forensics, and Windows internals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Network forensics experience, including packet capture and analysis</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Incident response experience, including workflow procedures, evidence gathering, and chain of custody handling</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enterprise architecture familiarity (Active Directory, SCCM, LDAP/RADIUS/TACACS+, two-factor authentication) and virtualization technology (VMware, Citrix, VDI)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with common hacking and exploitation tools and methodologies, malware families, and AV/IDS/IPS evasion techniques</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of Menlo Security competitors, including their solutions, strengths, and weaknesses</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency with AI-assisted sales and productivity tools (LLM-based research, drafting, and summarization) as part of your everyday workflow</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Self-directed, with the ability to prioritize and execute project tasks in a methodical, disciplined manner and set clear expectations with stakeholders and team members</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/\">LinkedIn</a>!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why Menlo?</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: <strong>Proactive Leadership</strong>, <strong>Straight Talk</strong>, <strong>United Impact</strong>, <strong>Elevated Talent</strong>, and <strong>Customer-Compelled</strong>. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability</strong>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>TO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.</strong></em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.\n\n\nSUMMARY\n\nThe Menlo Security Sales Engineer is a customer-focused, technical sales professional who provides guidance and support to prospective and current customers across the region. Partnering closely with Regional Sales Managers and channel partners, the Sales Engineer scopes, recommends, and demonstrates security-focused solutions that map to each customer's business needs and budget. Acting in a consultative capacity, they serve as a trusted technical resource for account teams, partners, and customers alike. The team uses AI-assisted tools throughout the sales cycle, from account research and call preparation to drafting technical responses, so more time goes to the customer conversation and less to administration.\n\n\n\n\nOUTCOMES & KPIS\n\nKey Outcome(s) Owned:\n\n - Technical wins on regional sales opportunities, from discovery through successful proof of concept to close.\n\n - Partner technical self-sufficiency across the assigned region.\n\nSuccess Metrics / KPIs (drafted, for hiring manager review):\n\n - Technical win rate on supported opportunities\n\n - Proof of concept conversion rate (POC to closed-won)\n\n - Average POC cycle time from kickoff to technical decision\n\n - Number of partner engineers enabled/certified per quarter\n\n - Quality of field feedback delivered to Product Management and Engineering (adoption of submitted insights)\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Articulate the benefits of Menlo Security solutions to both technical and non-technical audiences, and research the technical requirements of each opportunity to scope and architect a solution that meets the customer's needs.\n\n - Understand the customer's business drivers and map them to a Menlo Security solution that fits both their needs and their budget.\n\n - Lead proof of concept engagements on regional sales opportunities, including deployment and configuration of Menlo Security services or software, training users on the solutions, and acting as the interface between Sales and technical staff to resolve open issues.\n\n - Use AI-assisted tools to prepare for customer engagements (account research, competitive positioning) and to draft and refine technical documentation, RFP responses, and follow-up communications, applying your own judgment for accuracy and fit.\n\n - Work closely with regional Menlo Security partners to build partner self-sufficiency and drive partner-led opportunities.\n\n - Work closely with customers to grow and expand their implementation and integration of Menlo Security products.\n\n - Provide reporting and feedback on customer accounts and field activities to Sales, Product Management, and Engineering, using AI-generated call summaries and CRM enrichment to keep account records current with less manual effort.\n\n\nFUNCTIONAL COMPETENCIES\n\nRequired:\n\n - Bachelor's or Master's degree in Computer Science or a related discipline, or equivalent experience\n\n - Based in Singapore, with overnight travel throughout the region as needed\n\n - 4+ years of pre-sales experience in the computer networking or security space\n\n - Strong knowledge and hands-on experience across core areas including web proxy technologies, network security (firewalls, IDS/IPS, HTTP/SSL proxies), network engineering fundamentals (OSI model, IPv4/6, routing, switching, DNS, VLANs and subnetting), and email security and mail flow\n\n - Excellent written and oral communication skills, with the ability to articulate both the business value and the technical advantages of Menlo Security solutions\n\n - A strong sense of accountability and ownership, a proactive, get-it-done attitude, and a passion for continuous learning\n\nPreferred / Nice to Have:\n\n - Experience with malware analysis (static, delta, and dynamic/runtime approaches), sandboxing solutions, host-based forensics, and Windows internals\n\n - Network forensics experience, including packet capture and analysis\n\n - Incident response experience, including workflow procedures, evidence gathering, and chain of custody handling\n\n - Enterprise architecture familiarity (Active Directory, SCCM, LDAP/RADIUS/TACACS+, two-factor authentication) and virtualization technology (VMware, Citrix, VDI)\n\n - Familiarity with common hacking and exploitation tools and methodologies, malware families, and AV/IDS/IPS evasion techniques\n\n - Working knowledge of Menlo Security competitors, including their solutions, strengths, and weaknesses\n\n - Fluency with AI-assisted sales and productivity tools (LLM-based research, drafting, and summarization) as part of your everyday workflow\n\n - Self-directed, with the ability to prioritize and execute project tasks in a methodical, disciplined manner and set clear expectations with stakeholders and team members\n\n\n\nFollow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/!\n\nWhy Menlo?\n\nAt Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: Proactive Leadership, Straight Talk, United Impact, Elevated Talent, and Customer-Compelled. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.\n\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability.\n\nTO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"91b3151a-89a8-49b2-b076-9aa019003dd1","title":"Senior Business Development Representative - Public Sector","department":"BDR","team":"BDR","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"US - Distributed","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-27T16:30:45.068+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States of America"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/91b3151a-89a8-49b2-b076-9aa019003dd1","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/91b3151a-89a8-49b2-b076-9aa019003dd1/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.</p><h2><strong>Summary</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Senior Business Development Representative, Public Sector is on the front line with prospects, partners, and customers, generating qualified pipeline across Federal agencies, State and Local government, and Public Sector departments within commercial organizations. This role partners closely with Field Sales and Menlo's channel ecosystem of partners, resellers, and Federal System Integrators to open doors into some of the most security-conscious organizations in the world. The person in this role uses AI tools daily for account research, call preparation, and outreach drafting, so more of their time goes to real conversations with prospects and less to administrative work. It's a high-visibility role for someone who wants to build a career in cybersecurity sales while working with a market that genuinely needs what Menlo delivers.</p><h2><strong>Outcomes &amp; KPIs</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>(Metrics below are drafted suggestions for the hiring manager to confirm or adjust.)</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Outcome(s) Owned:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A consistent, growing flow of qualified Public Sector pipeline for the field sales team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep, well-nurtured engagement across the assigned target account list, in partnership with Field Sales and channel partners.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Success Metrics / KPIs:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Qualified meetings booked and held per month.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pipeline dollars sourced per quarter.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead-to-opportunity conversion rate in Salesforce.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Engagement coverage across Target Account Program accounts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prospect attendance sourced for targeted Menlo field events.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prospect into Public Sector accounts through cold calling and multi-channel outreach, qualify leads, and schedule meetings between qualified prospects and the sales team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use AI tools to research accounts, prepare for calls, and draft tailored outbound messaging, applying your own judgment for accuracy, tone, and public sector context.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deliver Menlo's pitch and technology story, tailoring it to the specific mission and needs of each prospect and answering questions clearly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage and nurture leads end to end in Salesforce, including tracking, follow-up, and conversion, using AI-generated call summaries and CRM enrichment to reduce administrative time.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with partners, resellers, and Federal System Integrators to expand Menlo's reach into Federal agencies, State and Local organizations, and Public Sector departments within commercial entities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support Target Account Programs to grow large Enterprise accounts, working closely with Field Sales to continuously nurture them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Invite and schedule prospects for targeted Menlo field events; some travel will be required.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Functional Competencies</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Required:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1-3 years of business development or sales development experience within the IT industry and/or selling cybersecurity or SaaS products, with a proven track record in cold calling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to understand technical information and explain it in simple, clear terms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency with Salesforce for tracking meetings, opportunities, and prospect details.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organization and time management skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's degree or equivalent experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Willingness to travel occasionally.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred / Nice to Have:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cybersecurity industry background.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of Public Sector agencies, budget and procurement cycles, and contract vehicles.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with prospecting and marketing automation tools such as <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Outreach.io\">Outreach.io</a>, ZoomInfo, or LinkedIn Sales Navigator.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience using AI sales tools for account research, outreach personalization, or call summarization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of sales and marketing principles and strategies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency with Microsoft Office and Google Workspace.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience thriving in a fast-paced, high-growth environment with constant learning.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Our Compensation and Benefits</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Menlo Security, Base Salary is one part of our competitive total compensation and benefits package and is determined using a salary range. The base salary range for this role is  $58,100 - $74,900.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In accordance with NY, CO, CA, and WA law, the range provided is Menlo Security’s reasonable estimate of the base compensation for this role. The actual amount may be higher or lower, based on non-discriminatory factors such as experience, knowledge, skills, abilities, and location. All employees may be eligible to become Menlo Security shareholders through eligibility for stock-based compensation grants, which are awarded to employees based on company and individual performance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security does not accept unsolicited resumes from search firm recruiters. Fees will not be paid in the event a candidate submitted by a recruiter without an agreement in place is hired; such resumes will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security is an equal opportunity employer. All aspects of employment will be based on merit, competence, performance, and business needs. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, marital status, age, national origin, ancestry, physical or mental disability, medical condition, pregnancy, genetic information, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, veteran status, or any other status protected under federal, state, or local law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">MSGL-I4</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/\">LinkedIn</a>!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why Menlo?</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: <strong>Proactive Leadership</strong>, <strong>Straight Talk</strong>, <strong>United Impact</strong>, <strong>Elevated Talent</strong>, and <strong>Customer-Compelled</strong>. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability</strong>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>TO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.</strong></em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.\n\n\nSUMMARY\n\nThe Senior Business Development Representative, Public Sector is on the front line with prospects, partners, and customers, generating qualified pipeline across Federal agencies, State and Local government, and Public Sector departments within commercial organizations. This role partners closely with Field Sales and Menlo's channel ecosystem of partners, resellers, and Federal System Integrators to open doors into some of the most security-conscious organizations in the world. The person in this role uses AI tools daily for account research, call preparation, and outreach drafting, so more of their time goes to real conversations with prospects and less to administrative work. It's a high-visibility role for someone who wants to build a career in cybersecurity sales while working with a market that genuinely needs what Menlo delivers.\n\n\nOUTCOMES & KPIS\n\n(Metrics below are drafted suggestions for the hiring manager to confirm or adjust.)\n\nKey Outcome(s) Owned:\n\n - A consistent, growing flow of qualified Public Sector pipeline for the field sales team.\n\n - Deep, well-nurtured engagement across the assigned target account list, in partnership with Field Sales and channel partners.\n\nSuccess Metrics / KPIs:\n\n - Qualified meetings booked and held per month.\n\n - Pipeline dollars sourced per quarter.\n\n - Lead-to-opportunity conversion rate in Salesforce.\n\n - Engagement coverage across Target Account Program accounts.\n\n - Prospect attendance sourced for targeted Menlo field events.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Prospect into Public Sector accounts through cold calling and multi-channel outreach, qualify leads, and schedule meetings between qualified prospects and the sales team.\n\n - Use AI tools to research accounts, prepare for calls, and draft tailored outbound messaging, applying your own judgment for accuracy, tone, and public sector context.\n\n - Deliver Menlo's pitch and technology story, tailoring it to the specific mission and needs of each prospect and answering questions clearly.\n\n - Manage and nurture leads end to end in Salesforce, including tracking, follow-up, and conversion, using AI-generated call summaries and CRM enrichment to reduce administrative time.\n\n - Work with partners, resellers, and Federal System Integrators to expand Menlo's reach into Federal agencies, State and Local organizations, and Public Sector departments within commercial entities.\n\n - Support Target Account Programs to grow large Enterprise accounts, working closely with Field Sales to continuously nurture them.\n\n - Invite and schedule prospects for targeted Menlo field events; some travel will be required.\n\n\nFUNCTIONAL COMPETENCIES\n\nRequired:\n\n - 1-3 years of business development or sales development experience within the IT industry and/or selling cybersecurity or SaaS products, with a proven track record in cold calling.\n\n - Ability to understand technical information and explain it in simple, clear terms.\n\n - Proficiency with Salesforce for tracking meetings, opportunities, and prospect details.\n\n - Strong organization and time management skills.\n\n - Bachelor's degree or equivalent experience.\n\n - Willingness to travel occasionally.\n\nPreferred / Nice to Have:\n\n - Cybersecurity industry background.\n\n - Knowledge of Public Sector agencies, budget and procurement cycles, and contract vehicles.\n\n - Experience with prospecting and marketing automation tools such as Outreach.io http://Outreach.io, ZoomInfo, or LinkedIn Sales Navigator.\n\n - Experience using AI sales tools for account research, outreach personalization, or call summarization.\n\n - Knowledge of sales and marketing principles and strategies.\n\n - Proficiency with Microsoft Office and Google Workspace.\n\n - Experience thriving in a fast-paced, high-growth environment with constant learning.\n\nOur Compensation and Benefits\n\nAt Menlo Security, Base Salary is one part of our competitive total compensation and benefits package and is determined using a salary range. The base salary range for this role is  $58,100 - $74,900.\n\nIn accordance with NY, CO, CA, and WA law, the range provided is Menlo Security’s reasonable estimate of the base compensation for this role. The actual amount may be higher or lower, based on non-discriminatory factors such as experience, knowledge, skills, abilities, and location. All employees may be eligible to become Menlo Security shareholders through eligibility for stock-based compensation grants, which are awarded to employees based on company and individual performance.\n\nMenlo Security does not accept unsolicited resumes from search firm recruiters. Fees will not be paid in the event a candidate submitted by a recruiter without an agreement in place is hired; such resumes will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. \n\nMenlo Security is an equal opportunity employer. All aspects of employment will be based on merit, competence, performance, and business needs. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, marital status, age, national origin, ancestry, physical or mental disability, medical condition, pregnancy, genetic information, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, veteran status, or any other status protected under federal, state, or local law.\n\n \n\nMSGL-I4\n\nFollow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/!\n\nWhy Menlo?\n\nAt Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: Proactive Leadership, Straight Talk, United Impact, Elevated Talent, and Customer-Compelled. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.\n\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability.\n\nTO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"786af3bb-1d59-495e-a665-cce6831d3dbd","title":"Senior Product Designer","department":"Prod Mgmt","team":"Prod Mgmt","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"APAC - India","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"APAC - India","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Bangalore","addressCountry":"India","addressLocality":"Bangalore"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-08-11T06:11:06.726+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Karnataka","addressCountry":"India","addressLocality":"Bangalore"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/786af3bb-1d59-495e-a665-cce6831d3dbd","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/786af3bb-1d59-495e-a665-cce6831d3dbd/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.</p><h2><strong>Summary</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security is on a mission to make the browser the most secure surface in the enterprise, protecting the world's most demanding organizations by stopping threats before they reach the endpoint. As a Senior Product Designer on the Browser &amp; Data Security team, you'll help shape the next generation of experiences across HEAT Shield, the Menlo Secure Extension, AI Adaptive DLP, Browsing Forensics, and the administrative surfaces that tie them together — turning enterprise-scale security complexity into experiences that feel simple and confident. You'll partner closely with product management, engineering, and fellow designers to own end-to-end journeys spanning policy management, monitoring, investigation, and configuration. The team weaves AI into both how Menlo builds its products and how those products defend customers, and you'll use AI-assisted design and prototyping tools to explore more directions, move faster, and raise the bar on high-fidelity concepts. This is a hybrid role based in Bangalore, where the design, product, and engineering org come together in person regularly, with flexibility to do focused work wherever works best.</p><h2><strong>Outcomes &amp; KPIs</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Outcome(s) Owned:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deliver intuitive, enterprise-grade design solutions across Menlo's browser and data security products that turn complex, high-density security data into clear, confident action for both end users and administrators.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Success Metrics / KPIs:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Usability outcomes (e.g., task success rate, SUS score) for shipped admin and end-user workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cycle time from business requirements to high-fidelity, engineering-ready prototypes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design system adoption and consistency across new feature launches.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stakeholder/leadership satisfaction with design reviews and \"North Star\" concepts.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design seamless, Chromium-based end-user experiences while architecting powerful, scalable management tooling for security administrators.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own complex, multi-step admin workflows — connection setup, domain and user-group configuration, conflict detection, and entitlement-aware, SKU-gated experiences — and make them feel effortless.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate dense telemetry (Last Mile Data Security, Browsing Forensics, DLP events) into dashboards and investigation flows that are actionable at a glance and powerful on a drill-down.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with product and engineering to turn business requirements into use cases, flows, wireframes, and high-fidelity, interactive prototypes — applying AI-assisted design and prototyping tools to move faster, explore more, and raise the bar on \"North Star\" concepts that feel like live products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Champion executive and stakeholder reviews, using storytelling and influence to align senior leaders on the product vision.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead and collaborate with UX research on exploratory and evaluative studies, and conduct product audits to uphold UX and design-system best practices, including accessibility.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to and help evolve the design system, and raise the design bar through documentation, onboarding experiences, clear handoffs, and design QA.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Functional Competencies</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Required:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of UX design experience, with a portfolio focused on high-fidelity web products and data-heavy, enterprise interfaces.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to design complex, high-density web dashboards that are accessible, actionable, and optimized for browser environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong systems thinking — able to distill ambiguous, complex requirements into elegant, scalable design solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A sharp aesthetic sense paired with rigorous attention to detail, and the ability to produce work that is presentation-ready for leadership.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong Figma foundations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of modern web technologies, enabling effective partnership with front-end engineering teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A collaborative, candid working style — gives and receives constructive feedback with humility and maturity, and is willing to fail fast, learn, and iterate.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to advocate for users through deep empathy and user-centered methods, while balancing technical constraints and business goals.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred / Nice to Have:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency or eagerness to grow in advanced prototyping, motion, and AI-assisted design tooling (e.g., Polymet, Lovable, Pendo, or similar).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing for, or strong interest in, security, browser, SaaS, or other technically complex domains; familiarity with admin/IT-facing products is a plus.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">MSGL-I4</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/\">LinkedIn</a>!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why Menlo?</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: <strong>Proactive Leadership</strong>, <strong>Straight Talk</strong>, <strong>United Impact</strong>, <strong>Elevated Talent</strong>, and <strong>Customer-Compelled</strong>. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability</strong>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>TO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.</strong></em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.\n\n\nSUMMARY\n\nMenlo Security is on a mission to make the browser the most secure surface in the enterprise, protecting the world's most demanding organizations by stopping threats before they reach the endpoint. As a Senior Product Designer on the Browser & Data Security team, you'll help shape the next generation of experiences across HEAT Shield, the Menlo Secure Extension, AI Adaptive DLP, Browsing Forensics, and the administrative surfaces that tie them together — turning enterprise-scale security complexity into experiences that feel simple and confident. You'll partner closely with product management, engineering, and fellow designers to own end-to-end journeys spanning policy management, monitoring, investigation, and configuration. The team weaves AI into both how Menlo builds its products and how those products defend customers, and you'll use AI-assisted design and prototyping tools to explore more directions, move faster, and raise the bar on high-fidelity concepts. This is a hybrid role based in Bangalore, where the design, product, and engineering org come together in person regularly, with flexibility to do focused work wherever works best.\n\n\nOUTCOMES & KPIS\n\nKey Outcome(s) Owned:\n\n - Deliver intuitive, enterprise-grade design solutions across Menlo's browser and data security products that turn complex, high-density security data into clear, confident action for both end users and administrators.\n\nSuccess Metrics / KPIs:\n\n - Usability outcomes (e.g., task success rate, SUS score) for shipped admin and end-user workflows.\n\n - Cycle time from business requirements to high-fidelity, engineering-ready prototypes.\n\n - Design system adoption and consistency across new feature launches.\n\n - Stakeholder/leadership satisfaction with design reviews and \"North Star\" concepts.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Design seamless, Chromium-based end-user experiences while architecting powerful, scalable management tooling for security administrators.\n\n - Own complex, multi-step admin workflows — connection setup, domain and user-group configuration, conflict detection, and entitlement-aware, SKU-gated experiences — and make them feel effortless.\n\n - Translate dense telemetry (Last Mile Data Security, Browsing Forensics, DLP events) into dashboards and investigation flows that are actionable at a glance and powerful on a drill-down.\n\n - Partner with product and engineering to turn business requirements into use cases, flows, wireframes, and high-fidelity, interactive prototypes — applying AI-assisted design and prototyping tools to move faster, explore more, and raise the bar on \"North Star\" concepts that feel like live products.\n\n - Champion executive and stakeholder reviews, using storytelling and influence to align senior leaders on the product vision.\n\n - Lead and collaborate with UX research on exploratory and evaluative studies, and conduct product audits to uphold UX and design-system best practices, including accessibility.\n\n - Contribute to and help evolve the design system, and raise the design bar through documentation, onboarding experiences, clear handoffs, and design QA.\n\n\nFUNCTIONAL COMPETENCIES\n\nRequired:\n\n - 4+ years of UX design experience, with a portfolio focused on high-fidelity web products and data-heavy, enterprise interfaces.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to design complex, high-density web dashboards that are accessible, actionable, and optimized for browser environments.\n\n - Strong systems thinking — able to distill ambiguous, complex requirements into elegant, scalable design solutions.\n\n - A sharp aesthetic sense paired with rigorous attention to detail, and the ability to produce work that is presentation-ready for leadership.\n\n - Strong Figma foundations.\n\n - Working knowledge of modern web technologies, enabling effective partnership with front-end engineering teams.\n\n - A collaborative, candid working style — gives and receives constructive feedback with humility and maturity, and is willing to fail fast, learn, and iterate.\n\n - Ability to advocate for users through deep empathy and user-centered methods, while balancing technical constraints and business goals.\n\nPreferred / Nice to Have:\n\n - Fluency or eagerness to grow in advanced prototyping, motion, and AI-assisted design tooling (e.g., Polymet, Lovable, Pendo, or similar).\n\n - Experience designing for, or strong interest in, security, browser, SaaS, or other technically complex domains; familiarity with admin/IT-facing products is a plus.\n\n\n\nMSGL-I4\n\nFollow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/!\n\nWhy Menlo?\n\nAt Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: Proactive Leadership, Straight Talk, United Impact, Elevated Talent, and Customer-Compelled. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.\n\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability.\n\nTO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"de57c573-7e23-47a1-ad4a-182296241aff","title":"External Post","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"EMEA - Israel","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-02T19:57:36.306+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Tel Aviv","addressCountry":"Israel","addressLocality":"Tel Aviv"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/de57c573-7e23-47a1-ad4a-182296241aff","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/de57c573-7e23-47a1-ad4a-182296241aff/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.</p><h2><strong>Summary</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a QA Engineer to join our engineering team and own quality across the software delivery lifecycle, from requirements review through release validation. In this role, you'll design and execute test strategies and build and maintain automated test suites, partnering closely with developers, product managers, and DevOps to ship stable, secure, and reliable releases. You'll also use AI-assisted testing tools to speed up test case generation, defect triage, and log analysis, freeing up more time to focus on the highest-risk areas of the product. This is a chance to shape quality practices for products that protect major global businesses from cyberattacks.</p><h2><strong>Outcomes &amp; KPIs</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Outcome(s) Owned:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Releases meet Menlo's quality, security, and reliability bar before reaching customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automated test coverage scales with the engineering team's release velocity.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Success Metrics / KPIs:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Defect escape rate to production, trending down quarter over quarter.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automated test coverage across critical-path and regression suites.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Average time from defect identification to verified resolution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Percentage of releases passing the quality gate on first pass.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Test cycle turnaround time relative to release cadence.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and execute comprehensive test plans, test cases, and test scenarios based on product requirements and technical specifications.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Perform manual and automated testing for web applications, APIs, and backend services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain automated test suites for regression, smoke, and critical-path coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Validate functional, integration, end-to-end, and non-functional requirements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use AI-assisted tools to help generate and maintain test cases and to triage flaky tests and analyze failure logs, speeding up root-cause identification.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify, document, prioritize, and track defects with clear reproduction steps and impact analysis.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with developers to troubleshoot issues and verify fixes quickly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in requirement and design reviews to catch quality risks early, and drive continuous improvements in QA processes and tooling.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Functional Competencies</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Required:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience in software quality assurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong knowledge of software testing methodologies, test design techniques, and SDLC/STLC.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with API testing tools such as Postman or similar.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with test automation frameworks and scripting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with bug tracking and test management tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of CI/CD workflows and version control systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical and problem-solving skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and verbal communication skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort incorporating AI-assisted tools (e.g., for test case generation, log analysis, or defect triage) into day-to-day QA workflows.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred / Nice to Have:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently and collaborate effectively in a fast-paced, cross-functional environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience testing cloud-native or microservices-based applications.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with performance or security testing tools and practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of containerized environments and orchestration platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to message queues, distributed systems, and event-driven architectures.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working in Agile or Scrum teams.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">MSGL-I4</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/\">LinkedIn</a>!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why Menlo?</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: <strong>Proactive Leadership</strong>, <strong>Straight Talk</strong>, <strong>United Impact</strong>, <strong>Elevated Talent</strong>, and <strong>Customer-Compelled</strong>. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability</strong>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>TO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.</strong></em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.\n\n\nSUMMARY\n\nWe're looking for a QA Engineer to join our engineering team and own quality across the software delivery lifecycle, from requirements review through release validation. In this role, you'll design and execute test strategies and build and maintain automated test suites, partnering closely with developers, product managers, and DevOps to ship stable, secure, and reliable releases. You'll also use AI-assisted testing tools to speed up test case generation, defect triage, and log analysis, freeing up more time to focus on the highest-risk areas of the product. This is a chance to shape quality practices for products that protect major global businesses from cyberattacks.\n\n\nOUTCOMES & KPIS\n\nKey Outcome(s) Owned:\n\n - Releases meet Menlo's quality, security, and reliability bar before reaching customers.\n\n - Automated test coverage scales with the engineering team's release velocity.\n\nSuccess Metrics / KPIs:\n\n - Defect escape rate to production, trending down quarter over quarter.\n\n - Automated test coverage across critical-path and regression suites.\n\n - Average time from defect identification to verified resolution.\n\n - Percentage of releases passing the quality gate on first pass.\n\n - Test cycle turnaround time relative to release cadence.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Design and execute comprehensive test plans, test cases, and test scenarios based on product requirements and technical specifications.\n\n - Perform manual and automated testing for web applications, APIs, and backend services.\n\n - Build and maintain automated test suites for regression, smoke, and critical-path coverage.\n\n - Validate functional, integration, end-to-end, and non-functional requirements.\n\n - Use AI-assisted tools to help generate and maintain test cases and to triage flaky tests and analyze failure logs, speeding up root-cause identification.\n\n - Identify, document, prioritize, and track defects with clear reproduction steps and impact analysis.\n\n - Collaborate with developers to troubleshoot issues and verify fixes quickly.\n\n - Participate in requirement and design reviews to catch quality risks early, and drive continuous improvements in QA processes and tooling.\n\n\nFUNCTIONAL COMPETENCIES\n\nRequired:\n\n - 3+ years of experience in software quality assurance.\n\n - Strong knowledge of software testing methodologies, test design techniques, and SDLC/STLC.\n\n - Hands-on experience with API testing tools such as Postman or similar.\n\n - Experience with test automation frameworks and scripting.\n\n - Familiarity with bug tracking and test management tools.\n\n - Understanding of CI/CD workflows and version control systems.\n\n - Strong analytical and problem-solving skills.\n\n - Excellent written and verbal communication skills.\n\n - Comfort incorporating AI-assisted tools (e.g., for test case generation, log analysis, or defect triage) into day-to-day QA workflows.\n\nPreferred / Nice to Have:\n\n - Ability to work independently and collaborate effectively in a fast-paced, cross-functional environment.\n\n - Experience testing cloud-native or microservices-based applications.\n\n - Experience with performance or security testing tools and practices.\n\n - Knowledge of containerized environments and orchestration platforms.\n\n - Exposure to message queues, distributed systems, and event-driven architectures.\n\n - Experience working in Agile or Scrum teams.\n\nMSGL-I4\n\nFollow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/!\n\nWhy Menlo?\n\nAt Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: Proactive Leadership, Straight Talk, United Impact, Elevated Talent, and Customer-Compelled. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.\n\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability.\n\nTO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"43b68d12-2371-48c8-91c7-e69d6d0aa9c2","title":"Senior Software Engineer (Chromium) ","department":"Oper","team":"Oper","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"EMEA - UK","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-13T13:18:56.997+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Berkshire","addressCountry":"United Kingdom","addressLocality":"Bracknell"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/43b68d12-2371-48c8-91c7-e69d6d0aa9c2","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/43b68d12-2371-48c8-91c7-e69d6d0aa9c2/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.</p><h2><strong>Summary</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security is looking for a Senior Software Engineer to join our Chromium engineering team in support of MARS, Menlo's internal AI initiative. You'll bring strong C++ skills — ideally with hands-on Chromium experience across layers such as content, browser, core, compositor, skia, and networking — to build and harden the browser capabilities that make Menlo's AI-driven features possible. The role blends deep systems and networking engineering with hands-on work on AI agents and MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers, alongside the cloud infrastructure (AWS, GCP, Kubernetes, Terraform, Linux) that supports them. You'll work alongside engineers across Chromium, AI, and security disciplines to ship reliable, high-performance capabilities, using AI-assisted development tools yourself to move faster without cutting corners on quality.<br /></p><h2><strong>Outcomes &amp; KPIs</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Outcome(s) Owned:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ship reliable, high-performance Chromium-based capabilities that power Menlo's internal AI/agent initiatives (MARS), while maintaining the security and performance bar expected of Menlo's browser platform.<br /></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Success Metrics / KPIs</strong>:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Feature delivery velocity against MARS roadmap milestones.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Performance and stability of shipped Chromium-based components (e.g., crash rate, latency).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reduction in manual toil via agent/MCP-based tooling adopted internally.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Code review turnaround time and quality for C++ contributions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Successful integration of AI agents or MCP servers into internal workflows or product surfaces.<br /></p></li></ul><h2><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, build, and maintain Chromium-based browser components in C++, working across layers such as content, browser, core, compositor, skia, and networking, that power Menlo's security and AI-driven capabilities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Apply strong networking fundamentals and HTTP security expertise to harden Menlo's browser isolation and network-facing infrastructure.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with the MARS team to build and integrate AI agent capabilities and MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers into Menlo's platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use Python or Rust to build supporting tooling, services, and prototypes alongside core C++ work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deploy and operate the cloud infrastructure (AWS, GCP) and orchestration (Kubernetes, Terraform) needed to run agent/MCP workloads reliably.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Debug and optimize performance-critical, high-scale systems across the browser and supporting infrastructure.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate cross-functionally with product, security, and AI engineering teams to ship capabilities end-to-end.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Apply AI-assisted coding tools to accelerate development, testing, and code review as part of your daily workflow.<br /></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Functional Competencies</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Required:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong C++ engineering skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong networking fundamentals, including solid knowledge of HTTP security.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's degree or higher in Computer Science or a related field.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred / Nice to Have:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience across Chromium layers such as content, browser, core, compositor, skia, and networking (or equivalent large-scale, high-performance C++ systems experience).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Python or Rust experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building or integrating AI agents and MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with AWS, GCP, Terraform, Kubernetes, and Linux.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Tornado, HAProxy, and AWS EC2.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> </p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">MSGL-I4</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/\">LinkedIn</a>!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why Menlo?</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: <strong>Proactive Leadership</strong>, <strong>Straight Talk</strong>, <strong>United Impact</strong>, <strong>Elevated Talent</strong>, and <strong>Customer-Compelled</strong>. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability</strong>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>TO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.</strong></em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.\n\n\nSUMMARY\n\nMenlo Security is looking for a Senior Software Engineer to join our Chromium engineering team in support of MARS, Menlo's internal AI initiative. You'll bring strong C++ skills — ideally with hands-on Chromium experience across layers such as content, browser, core, compositor, skia, and networking — to build and harden the browser capabilities that make Menlo's AI-driven features possible. The role blends deep systems and networking engineering with hands-on work on AI agents and MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers, alongside the cloud infrastructure (AWS, GCP, Kubernetes, Terraform, Linux) that supports them. You'll work alongside engineers across Chromium, AI, and security disciplines to ship reliable, high-performance capabilities, using AI-assisted development tools yourself to move faster without cutting corners on quality.\n\n\n\nOUTCOMES & KPIS\n\nKey Outcome(s) Owned:\n\n - Ship reliable, high-performance Chromium-based capabilities that power Menlo's internal AI/agent initiatives (MARS), while maintaining the security and performance bar expected of Menlo's browser platform.\n   \n\nSuccess Metrics / KPIs:\n\n - Feature delivery velocity against MARS roadmap milestones.\n\n - Performance and stability of shipped Chromium-based components (e.g., crash rate, latency).\n\n - Reduction in manual toil via agent/MCP-based tooling adopted internally.\n\n - Code review turnaround time and quality for C++ contributions.\n\n - Successful integration of AI agents or MCP servers into internal workflows or product surfaces.\n   \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Design, build, and maintain Chromium-based browser components in C++, working across layers such as content, browser, core, compositor, skia, and networking, that power Menlo's security and AI-driven capabilities.\n\n - Apply strong networking fundamentals and HTTP security expertise to harden Menlo's browser isolation and network-facing infrastructure.\n\n - Partner with the MARS team to build and integrate AI agent capabilities and MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers into Menlo's platform.\n\n - Use Python or Rust to build supporting tooling, services, and prototypes alongside core C++ work.\n\n - Deploy and operate the cloud infrastructure (AWS, GCP) and orchestration (Kubernetes, Terraform) needed to run agent/MCP workloads reliably.\n\n - Debug and optimize performance-critical, high-scale systems across the browser and supporting infrastructure.\n\n - Collaborate cross-functionally with product, security, and AI engineering teams to ship capabilities end-to-end.\n\n - Apply AI-assisted coding tools to accelerate development, testing, and code review as part of your daily workflow.\n   \n\n\nFUNCTIONAL COMPETENCIES\n\nRequired:\n\n - Strong C++ engineering skills\n\n - Strong networking fundamentals, including solid knowledge of HTTP security.\n\n - Bachelor's degree or higher in Computer Science or a related field.\n\nPreferred / Nice to Have:\n\n - Experience across Chromium layers such as content, browser, core, compositor, skia, and networking (or equivalent large-scale, high-performance C++ systems experience).\n\n - Python or Rust experience.\n\n - Experience building or integrating AI agents and MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers.\n\n - Experience with AWS, GCP, Terraform, Kubernetes, and Linux.\n\n - Experience with Tornado, HAProxy, and AWS EC2.\n   \n    \n\nMSGL-I4\n\nFollow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/!\n\nWhy Menlo?\n\nAt Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: Proactive Leadership, Straight Talk, United Impact, Elevated Talent, and Customer-Compelled. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.\n\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability.\n\nTO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"26986f1d-4667-4559-a57b-9758d6aa0ec8","title":"Senior Engineer I (Auth) ","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"AMER - Canada","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-17T17:18:23.080+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Canada"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/26986f1d-4667-4559-a57b-9758d6aa0ec8","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/26986f1d-4667-4559-a57b-9758d6aa0ec8/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.</p><h2><strong>Summary</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security is hiring a Senior Software Engineer to own and evolve our Authentication Service — the layer that every user request and AI agent request flows through before anything else happens. Authentication is foundational to how our browser security product works, which means the decisions made here have direct consequences for security posture, system performance, and how Menlo's platform can grow. You will work with a team that has deep context on this system, taking full ownership from design through deployment on services that protect enterprise customers at scale. This role sits at the intersection of systems engineering and security, and it is increasingly central to how Menlo secures AI agent access in enterprise environments — a fast-moving and technically interesting problem space.<br /></p><h2><strong>Outcomes &amp; KPIs</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Outcome(s) Owned:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable, secure, and performant authentication services that correctly handle every user and AI agent request flowing through the Menlo platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Full lifecycle ownership of assigned services, from design and implementation through deployment and ongoing operation.<br /></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Success Metrics / KPIs:</strong> <em>(drafted for hiring manager review and adjustment)</em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Authentication service availability and latency meeting or exceeding defined SLOs under production load.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Zero critical security vulnerabilities shipped to production in owned code, measured by post-release security review outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Test coverage and failure-scenario validation maintained or improved across owned code paths.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Features delivered on committed roadmap dates, with defect and rollback rates tracked post-release.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">AI agent authentication capabilities shipped in alignment with the Agentic protection roadmap.<br /></p></li></ul><h2><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, build, and own production services in the Authentication Service, with direct responsibility for correctness, scalability, and security from day one.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and extend Menlo's AI agent authentication capabilities, ensuring the platform can securely govern how AI agents authenticate and access enterprise resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Optimize for latency and throughput in networked applications, using profiling tools and efficient concurrency models to handle demanding production workloads.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Apply rigorous security engineering practices — including threat modeling and vulnerability mitigation — to protect data integrity across distributed environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use AI coding and debugging tools as part of your development workflow, while critically evaluating outputs for correctness, security implications, and long-term architectural fit before they land in production.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner cross-functionally with product, security, and AI engineering teams to ship authentication capabilities end to end.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Write comprehensive unit and integration tests covering failure scenarios, and conduct code and design reviews for peers.<br /></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Functional Competencies</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Required:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience building and operating production systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience in Rust, Python, or Go in a production environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to optimize networked applications for latency and throughput using profiling and concurrency techniques.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong background in security-oriented engineering: threat modeling, vulnerability mitigation, and data integrity in distributed systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of comprehensive testing — unit, integration, and failure-scenario coverage — as a normal part of shipping.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Practical fluency with AI coding assistants, with the judgment to critically assess outputs rather than accepting them uncritically.<br /></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred / Nice to Have:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with authentication standards and protocols such as OAuth, OIDC, or SAML.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to AI agent systems, agentic frameworks, or machine-to-machine authentication patterns.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working on foundational platform or infrastructure services where correctness is non-negotiable.<br /></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Our Compensation and Benefits</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Menlo Security, Base Salary is one part of our competitive total compensation and benefits package and is determined using a salary range. The base salary range for this role is 112,000 CAD - 168,000 CAD.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In accordance with Canadian law, the range provided is Menlo Security’s reasonable estimate of the base compensation for this role. The actual amount may be higher or lower, based on non-discriminatory factors such as experience, knowledge, skills, abilities, and location. All employees may be eligible to become Menlo Security shareholders through eligibility for stock-based compensation grants, which are awarded to employees based on company and individual performance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security does not accept unsolicited resumes from search firm recruiters. Fees will not be paid in the event a candidate submitted by a recruiter without an agreement in place is hired; such resumes will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security is an equal opportunity employer. All aspects of employment will be based on merit, competence, performance, and business needs. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, marital status, age, national origin, ancestry, physical or mental disability, medical condition, pregnancy, genetic information, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, veteran status, or any other status protected under federal, state, or local law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">MSGL-I4</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/\">LinkedIn</a>!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why Menlo?</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: <strong>Proactive Leadership</strong>, <strong>Straight Talk</strong>, <strong>United Impact</strong>, <strong>Elevated Talent</strong>, and <strong>Customer-Compelled</strong>. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability</strong>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>TO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.</strong></em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.\n\n\nSUMMARY\n\nMenlo Security is hiring a Senior Software Engineer to own and evolve our Authentication Service — the layer that every user request and AI agent request flows through before anything else happens. Authentication is foundational to how our browser security product works, which means the decisions made here have direct consequences for security posture, system performance, and how Menlo's platform can grow. You will work with a team that has deep context on this system, taking full ownership from design through deployment on services that protect enterprise customers at scale. This role sits at the intersection of systems engineering and security, and it is increasingly central to how Menlo secures AI agent access in enterprise environments — a fast-moving and technically interesting problem space.\n\n\n\nOUTCOMES & KPIS\n\nKey Outcome(s) Owned:\n\n - Reliable, secure, and performant authentication services that correctly handle every user and AI agent request flowing through the Menlo platform.\n\n - Full lifecycle ownership of assigned services, from design and implementation through deployment and ongoing operation.\n   \n\nSuccess Metrics / KPIs: (drafted for hiring manager review and adjustment)\n\n - Authentication service availability and latency meeting or exceeding defined SLOs under production load.\n\n - Zero critical security vulnerabilities shipped to production in owned code, measured by post-release security review outcomes.\n\n - Test coverage and failure-scenario validation maintained or improved across owned code paths.\n\n - Features delivered on committed roadmap dates, with defect and rollback rates tracked post-release.\n\n - AI agent authentication capabilities shipped in alignment with the Agentic protection roadmap.\n   \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Design, build, and own production services in the Authentication Service, with direct responsibility for correctness, scalability, and security from day one.\n\n - Develop and extend Menlo's AI agent authentication capabilities, ensuring the platform can securely govern how AI agents authenticate and access enterprise resources.\n\n - Optimize for latency and throughput in networked applications, using profiling tools and efficient concurrency models to handle demanding production workloads.\n\n - Apply rigorous security engineering practices — including threat modeling and vulnerability mitigation — to protect data integrity across distributed environments.\n\n - Use AI coding and debugging tools as part of your development workflow, while critically evaluating outputs for correctness, security implications, and long-term architectural fit before they land in production.\n\n - Partner cross-functionally with product, security, and AI engineering teams to ship authentication capabilities end to end.\n\n - Write comprehensive unit and integration tests covering failure scenarios, and conduct code and design reviews for peers.\n   \n\n\nFUNCTIONAL COMPETENCIES\n\nRequired:\n\n - 3+ years of experience building and operating production systems.\n\n - Hands-on experience in Rust, Python, or Go in a production environment.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to optimize networked applications for latency and throughput using profiling and concurrency techniques.\n\n - Strong background in security-oriented engineering: threat modeling, vulnerability mitigation, and data integrity in distributed systems.\n\n - Track record of comprehensive testing — unit, integration, and failure-scenario coverage — as a normal part of shipping.\n\n - Practical fluency with AI coding assistants, with the judgment to critically assess outputs rather than accepting them uncritically.\n   \n\nPreferred / Nice to Have:\n\n - Experience with authentication standards and protocols such as OAuth, OIDC, or SAML.\n\n - Exposure to AI agent systems, agentic frameworks, or machine-to-machine authentication patterns.\n\n - Experience working on foundational platform or infrastructure services where correctness is non-negotiable.\n   \n\nOur Compensation and Benefits\n\nAt Menlo Security, Base Salary is one part of our competitive total compensation and benefits package and is determined using a salary range. The base salary range for this role is 112,000 CAD - 168,000 CAD.\n\nIn accordance with Canadian law, the range provided is Menlo Security’s reasonable estimate of the base compensation for this role. The actual amount may be higher or lower, based on non-discriminatory factors such as experience, knowledge, skills, abilities, and location. All employees may be eligible to become Menlo Security shareholders through eligibility for stock-based compensation grants, which are awarded to employees based on company and individual performance.\n\nMenlo Security does not accept unsolicited resumes from search firm recruiters. Fees will not be paid in the event a candidate submitted by a recruiter without an agreement in place is hired; such resumes will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. \n\nMenlo Security is an equal opportunity employer. All aspects of employment will be based on merit, competence, performance, and business needs. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, marital status, age, national origin, ancestry, physical or mental disability, medical condition, pregnancy, genetic information, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, veteran status, or any other status protected under federal, state, or local law.\n\n \n\nMSGL-I4\n\nFollow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/!\n\nWhy Menlo?\n\nAt Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: Proactive Leadership, Straight Talk, United Impact, Elevated Talent, and Customer-Compelled. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.\n\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability.\n\nTO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"a9709f2a-5de6-4402-ac4c-24a196eff23e","title":"Senior Software Engineer I ","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"APAC - India","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-06T10:12:05.672+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Karnataka","addressCountry":"India","addressLocality":"Bangalore"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/a9709f2a-5de6-4402-ac4c-24a196eff23e","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/a9709f2a-5de6-4402-ac4c-24a196eff23e/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.</p><h2><strong>Summary</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security is hiring a Senior Software Engineer to join our growing Threat Protection and ShadowAI team in Bangalore. This team makes sure our users can safely browse the web through our secure cloud, protecting them from malicious sites (including those built or operated with AI) and securing access to authorized web applications. The services this team builds are a core part of Menlo's secure enterprise browser for both humans and AI agents, which means you will be working directly on one of the fastest-moving problems in security today: how organizations get visibility into and control over unsanctioned AI use without shutting it down. The team also uses AI in how it builds, from code assistants and AI-assisted test generation through to LLM-supported log and incident analysis, so you will be applying these tools as well as defending against their misuse. If you like distributed systems, deep technical problems, and work where the threat landscape changes month to month, this is a strong fit.</p><h2><strong>Outcomes &amp; KPIs</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Outcome(s) Owned:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable, performant delivery of Threat Protection and ShadowAI services that detect and control risky web and generative AI application usage for Menlo customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">End to end ownership of assigned features, from design through production operation and iteration.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Success Metrics / KPIs:</strong> </p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Service availability and latency for owned components meet or exceed team SLOs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Features delivered on committed roadmap dates, with quality measured by post-release defect and rollback rates.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automated test coverage maintained or improved on owned code paths.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Detection accuracy for AI application and malicious site coverage, measured by false positive and false negative rates.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mean time to detect and resolve production issues in owned services.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, develop, and own new features and services in the Threat Protection and ShadowAI product area, contributing directly to Menlo's technical roadmap.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build highly available, scalable distributed systems and APIs, including multithreaded and asynchronous applications, with performance and security considered from the start.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and refine the detection and policy capabilities that give customers visibility into generative AI and unsanctioned web application usage in their environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in building, deploying, and operating the Menlo Security platform in production, using dashboards, error reporting, metrics, and AI-assisted log and trace analysis to find and resolve defects quickly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use AI code assistants and AI-assisted test generation as part of your normal workflow to move faster, while applying your own judgment on correctness, security, and maintainability before anything ships.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with product, security, operations, and other cross-functional stakeholders to align on requirements, tradeoffs, and schedules.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Write unit and automated tests, conduct code and design reviews for peers, and evaluate emerging technologies that could improve our products.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Functional Competencies</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Required:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3-5 years of professional software development experience with one or more of NodeJS, Go, or Python.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3-5 years of hands on experience with cloud services such as GCP and/or AWS.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working experience with Linux and standard development tooling such as git.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Degree in Computer Science or a related field (BE, BTech, or Masters).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Practical fluency with AI coding and debugging assistants, including sound judgment about when to rely on LLM output and when to verify it independently.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Self-directed approach to problem solving, with the ability to pick up unfamiliar systems and technologies with limited guidance.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred / Nice to Have:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building large scale web applications and REST APIs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong grounding in complex data structures and database technologies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with containers, Docker, and Kubernetes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with cloud infrastructure as code tooling such as Terraform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with the Tornado web application framework and test automation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of adapting and improving engineering practices such as test driven development, continuous delivery, agile ceremonies, automation, and maintainable, testable code.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interest in or exposure to security, threat detection, or AI governance and safety.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Well organized and thorough, with strong attention to detail and documentation. </p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">MSGL-I4</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/\">LinkedIn</a>!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why Menlo?</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: <strong>Proactive Leadership</strong>, <strong>Straight Talk</strong>, <strong>United Impact</strong>, <strong>Elevated Talent</strong>, and <strong>Customer-Compelled</strong>. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability</strong>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>TO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.</strong></em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.\n\n\nSUMMARY\n\nMenlo Security is hiring a Senior Software Engineer to join our growing Threat Protection and ShadowAI team in Bangalore. This team makes sure our users can safely browse the web through our secure cloud, protecting them from malicious sites (including those built or operated with AI) and securing access to authorized web applications. The services this team builds are a core part of Menlo's secure enterprise browser for both humans and AI agents, which means you will be working directly on one of the fastest-moving problems in security today: how organizations get visibility into and control over unsanctioned AI use without shutting it down. The team also uses AI in how it builds, from code assistants and AI-assisted test generation through to LLM-supported log and incident analysis, so you will be applying these tools as well as defending against their misuse. If you like distributed systems, deep technical problems, and work where the threat landscape changes month to month, this is a strong fit.\n\n\nOUTCOMES & KPIS\n\nKey Outcome(s) Owned:\n\n - Reliable, performant delivery of Threat Protection and ShadowAI services that detect and control risky web and generative AI application usage for Menlo customers.\n\n - End to end ownership of assigned features, from design through production operation and iteration.\n\nSuccess Metrics / KPIs: \n\n - Service availability and latency for owned components meet or exceed team SLOs.\n\n - Features delivered on committed roadmap dates, with quality measured by post-release defect and rollback rates.\n\n - Automated test coverage maintained or improved on owned code paths.\n\n - Detection accuracy for AI application and malicious site coverage, measured by false positive and false negative rates.\n\n - Mean time to detect and resolve production issues in owned services.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Design, develop, and own new features and services in the Threat Protection and ShadowAI product area, contributing directly to Menlo's technical roadmap.\n\n - Build highly available, scalable distributed systems and APIs, including multithreaded and asynchronous applications, with performance and security considered from the start.\n\n - Build and refine the detection and policy capabilities that give customers visibility into generative AI and unsanctioned web application usage in their environments.\n\n - Participate in building, deploying, and operating the Menlo Security platform in production, using dashboards, error reporting, metrics, and AI-assisted log and trace analysis to find and resolve defects quickly.\n\n - Use AI code assistants and AI-assisted test generation as part of your normal workflow to move faster, while applying your own judgment on correctness, security, and maintainability before anything ships.\n\n - Partner with product, security, operations, and other cross-functional stakeholders to align on requirements, tradeoffs, and schedules.\n\n - Write unit and automated tests, conduct code and design reviews for peers, and evaluate emerging technologies that could improve our products.\n\n\nFUNCTIONAL COMPETENCIES\n\nRequired:\n\n - 3-5 years of professional software development experience with one or more of NodeJS, Go, or Python.\n\n - 3-5 years of hands on experience with cloud services such as GCP and/or AWS.\n\n - Working experience with Linux and standard development tooling such as git.\n\n - Degree in Computer Science or a related field (BE, BTech, or Masters).\n\n - Practical fluency with AI coding and debugging assistants, including sound judgment about when to rely on LLM output and when to verify it independently.\n\n - Self-directed approach to problem solving, with the ability to pick up unfamiliar systems and technologies with limited guidance.\n\nPreferred / Nice to Have:\n\n - Experience building large scale web applications and REST APIs.\n\n - Strong grounding in complex data structures and database technologies.\n\n - Experience with containers, Docker, and Kubernetes.\n\n - Experience with cloud infrastructure as code tooling such as Terraform.\n\n - Familiarity with the Tornado web application framework and test automation.\n\n - Track record of adapting and improving engineering practices such as test driven development, continuous delivery, agile ceremonies, automation, and maintainable, testable code.\n\n - Interest in or exposure to security, threat detection, or AI governance and safety.\n\n - Well organized and thorough, with strong attention to detail and documentation. \n\n\n\nMSGL-I4\n\nFollow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/!\n\nWhy Menlo?\n\nAt Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: Proactive Leadership, Straight Talk, United Impact, Elevated Talent, and Customer-Compelled. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.\n\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability.\n\nTO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"1aca00c9-c139-4dc8-aacb-4180f36a149f","title":"Senior Software Engineer","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"EMEA - UK","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-13T13:30:53.791+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Berkshire","addressCountry":"United Kingdom","addressLocality":"Bracknell"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/1aca00c9-c139-4dc8-aacb-4180f36a149f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/1aca00c9-c139-4dc8-aacb-4180f36a149f/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.</p><h2><strong>Summary</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security is hiring a Senior Software Engineer to join our Threat Protection and ShadowAI team in the UK. This team ensures that users can safely browse the web through Menlo's secure cloud — protecting them from malicious sites (including those built or operated with AI) and securing access to authorised web applications. The services this team builds are core to Menlo's secure enterprise browser for both humans and AI agents, which puts you at the centre of one of the most active problems in enterprise security right now: how organisations gain visibility into and control over unsanctioned AI usage without blocking it entirely. The team applies AI in how it builds as well — code assistants, AI-assisted test generation, and LLM-supported log and incident analysis — so you will be using these tools alongside defending against their misuse.<br /></p><h2><strong>Outcomes &amp; KPIs</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Outcome(s) Owned:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable, performant delivery of Threat Protection and ShadowAI services that detect and control risky web and generative AI application usage for Menlo customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">End-to-end ownership of assigned features, from design through production operation and iteration.<br /></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Success Metrics / KPIs:</strong> <em>(drafted for hiring manager review and adjustment)</em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Service availability and latency for owned components meet or exceed team SLOs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Features delivered on committed roadmap dates, with quality measured by post-release defect and rollback rates.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automated test coverage maintained or improved on owned code paths.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Detection accuracy for AI application and malicious site coverage, measured by false positive and false negative rates.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mean time to detect and resolve production issues in owned services.<br /></p></li></ul><h2><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, develop, and own new features and services in the Threat Protection and ShadowAI product area, contributing directly to Menlo's technical roadmap.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build highly available, scalable distributed systems and APIs, including multithreaded and asynchronous applications, with performance and security considered from the start.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and refine the detection and policy capabilities that give customers visibility into generative AI and unsanctioned web application usage in their environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in building, deploying, and operating the Menlo Security platform in production, using dashboards, error reporting, metrics, and AI-assisted log and trace analysis to identify and resolve defects quickly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use AI code assistants and AI-assisted test generation as part of your normal workflow to move faster, while applying your own judgement on correctness, security, and maintainability before anything ships.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with product, security, operations, and other cross-functional stakeholders to align on requirements, tradeoffs, and schedules.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Write unit and automated tests, conduct code and design reviews for peers, and evaluate emerging technologies that could improve our products.<br /></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Functional Competencies</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Required:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3-5 years of professional software development experience with one or more of NodeJS, Go, or Python.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3-5 years of hands-on experience with cloud services such as GCP and/or AWS.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working experience with Linux and standard development tooling such as git.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Degree in Computer Science or a related field (BE, BTech, or Masters), or equivalent practical experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Practical fluency with AI coding and debugging assistants, including sound judgement about when to rely on LLM output and when to verify it independently.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Self-directed approach to problem solving, with the ability to pick up unfamiliar systems and technologies with limited guidance.<br /></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred / Nice to Have:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building large-scale web applications and REST APIs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong grounding in complex data structures and database technologies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with containers, Docker, and Kubernetes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with cloud infrastructure as code tooling such as Terraform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with the Tornado web application framework and test automation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of adapting and improving engineering practices such as test-driven development, continuous delivery, agile ceremonies, automation, and maintainable, testable code.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interest in or exposure to security, threat detection, or AI governance and safety.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> </p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">MSGL-I4</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/\">LinkedIn</a>!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why Menlo?</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: <strong>Proactive Leadership</strong>, <strong>Straight Talk</strong>, <strong>United Impact</strong>, <strong>Elevated Talent</strong>, and <strong>Customer-Compelled</strong>. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability</strong>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>TO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.</strong></em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.\n\n\nSUMMARY\n\nMenlo Security is hiring a Senior Software Engineer to join our Threat Protection and ShadowAI team in the UK. This team ensures that users can safely browse the web through Menlo's secure cloud — protecting them from malicious sites (including those built or operated with AI) and securing access to authorised web applications. The services this team builds are core to Menlo's secure enterprise browser for both humans and AI agents, which puts you at the centre of one of the most active problems in enterprise security right now: how organisations gain visibility into and control over unsanctioned AI usage without blocking it entirely. The team applies AI in how it builds as well — code assistants, AI-assisted test generation, and LLM-supported log and incident analysis — so you will be using these tools alongside defending against their misuse.\n\n\n\nOUTCOMES & KPIS\n\nKey Outcome(s) Owned:\n\n - Reliable, performant delivery of Threat Protection and ShadowAI services that detect and control risky web and generative AI application usage for Menlo customers.\n\n - End-to-end ownership of assigned features, from design through production operation and iteration.\n   \n\nSuccess Metrics / KPIs: (drafted for hiring manager review and adjustment)\n\n - Service availability and latency for owned components meet or exceed team SLOs.\n\n - Features delivered on committed roadmap dates, with quality measured by post-release defect and rollback rates.\n\n - Automated test coverage maintained or improved on owned code paths.\n\n - Detection accuracy for AI application and malicious site coverage, measured by false positive and false negative rates.\n\n - Mean time to detect and resolve production issues in owned services.\n   \n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Design, develop, and own new features and services in the Threat Protection and ShadowAI product area, contributing directly to Menlo's technical roadmap.\n\n - Build highly available, scalable distributed systems and APIs, including multithreaded and asynchronous applications, with performance and security considered from the start.\n\n - Build and refine the detection and policy capabilities that give customers visibility into generative AI and unsanctioned web application usage in their environments.\n\n - Participate in building, deploying, and operating the Menlo Security platform in production, using dashboards, error reporting, metrics, and AI-assisted log and trace analysis to identify and resolve defects quickly.\n\n - Use AI code assistants and AI-assisted test generation as part of your normal workflow to move faster, while applying your own judgement on correctness, security, and maintainability before anything ships.\n\n - Partner with product, security, operations, and other cross-functional stakeholders to align on requirements, tradeoffs, and schedules.\n\n - Write unit and automated tests, conduct code and design reviews for peers, and evaluate emerging technologies that could improve our products.\n   \n\n\nFUNCTIONAL COMPETENCIES\n\nRequired:\n\n - 3-5 years of professional software development experience with one or more of NodeJS, Go, or Python.\n\n - 3-5 years of hands-on experience with cloud services such as GCP and/or AWS.\n\n - Working experience with Linux and standard development tooling such as git.\n\n - Degree in Computer Science or a related field (BE, BTech, or Masters), or equivalent practical experience.\n\n - Practical fluency with AI coding and debugging assistants, including sound judgement about when to rely on LLM output and when to verify it independently.\n\n - Self-directed approach to problem solving, with the ability to pick up unfamiliar systems and technologies with limited guidance.\n   \n\nPreferred / Nice to Have:\n\n - Experience building large-scale web applications and REST APIs.\n\n - Strong grounding in complex data structures and database technologies.\n\n - Experience with containers, Docker, and Kubernetes.\n\n - Experience with cloud infrastructure as code tooling such as Terraform.\n\n - Familiarity with the Tornado web application framework and test automation.\n\n - Track record of adapting and improving engineering practices such as test-driven development, continuous delivery, agile ceremonies, automation, and maintainable, testable code.\n\n - Interest in or exposure to security, threat detection, or AI governance and safety.\n   \n    \n\nMSGL-I4\n\nFollow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/!\n\nWhy Menlo?\n\nAt Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: Proactive Leadership, Straight Talk, United Impact, Elevated Talent, and Customer-Compelled. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.\n\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability.\n\nTO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"165467d7-5b6d-496b-97a5-0868d2595152","title":"Customer Success Manager - Japan","department":"Customer Success","team":"Customer Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"APAC - Japan","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-20T15:59:46.428+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Kanto","addressCountry":"Japan","addressLocality":"Tokyo"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/165467d7-5b6d-496b-97a5-0868d2595152","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/menlosecurity/165467d7-5b6d-496b-97a5-0868d2595152/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.</p><h2><strong>Summary</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a Senior Customer Success Manager to own the strategic relationship with our largest and most complex enterprise customers across Japan. You'll be the primary point of contact and trusted advisor for your portfolio, working closely with deployment, sales, and engineering teams to ensure customers realize maximum value from Menlo's isolation platform, and you'll be looked to as a source of judgment when accounts get complicated. You'll balance deep technical fluency with business acumen—using AI tools to accelerate account research and customer communication—so you can focus your energy on the strategic conversations that drive retention and expansion. You'll be bilingual in English and Japanese, comfortable traveling to customer sites, and someone junior CSMs can learn from.</p><h2><strong>Outcomes &amp; KPIs</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Outcome(s) Owned:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customer retention and net revenue retention (NRR) across a portfolio of strategic, high-complexity accounts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Successful deployment and adoption of Menlo solutions, with customers reaching their defined value milestones</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Uplift in team-wide execution through mentorship and playbook contributions that other CSMs rely on</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Success Metrics / KPIs:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Net retention rate (NRR) and expansion revenue for your book of business</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customer satisfaction scores and NPS feedback from your accounts (QBRs, surveys, touchpoints)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deployment success rate and time-to-value for implementations you support</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Forecast accuracy for customer renewals and expansion opportunities in your portfolio</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribution to team enablement: playbooks authored, peers mentored, workshops led</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the strategic relationship with enterprise customers across Japan, serving as the senior technical advisor and business partner to CTOs, CISOs, Security Architects, and Security Engineers, including at the most complex or highest-visibility accounts in the region.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead quarterly business reviews (QBRs) and executive touchpoints independently, presenting Menlo cloud security assessments with tailored, forward-looking recommendations; use AI-assisted meeting summaries and CRM enrichment to track progress and inform strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and build the business case for expansion opportunities using data-driven insights and AI-powered account research, and work with sales to convert them into upsell and cross-sell revenue.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Anticipate deployment and adoption risk before it surfaces; partner with technical teams on system design, configuration, and resiliency, and author or refine the Statements of Work (SOWs) and playbooks that guide implementations across the team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and deliver region-based workshops and user groups that enable customers on product capabilities, drawing on AI tools to synthesize feedback patterns and relay actionable insight to product and engineering teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner cross-functionally with sales and pre-sales leadership to shape account strategy, support renewals, and represent the voice of the Japan customer base in broader planning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish and maintain working relationships with key regional partners to effectively manage renewal opportunities</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Functional Competencies</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Required:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8–10+ years of experience in a customer-facing technical role (e.g., Customer Success Manager, Technical Account Manager, Sales Engineer, Solutions Engineer, or equivalent), with a track record on complex, high-value accounts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Native or near-native fluency in Japanese (written and verbal), sufficient to read complex contracts or technical documentation and negotiate, present to, and build trust with senior executive stakeholders without relying on translation or simplification</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional fluency in English for internal collaboration</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep knowledge of network security technologies: proxies, firewalls (NG/traditional), SSL/TLS, IPSec, SSO (SAML, OAuth, LDAP), MDM, Cloud APIs, SIEM, DLP, and CASB gateways.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated success supporting and deploying security solutions for large or high-complexity enterprise customers, including navigating multi-stakeholder, multi-team environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication skills and proven comfort presenting to and influencing executive-level audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong project management and organizational skills; able to manage a demanding portfolio and competing priorities without close oversight.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Willingness to travel to customer sites (up to 30%) and participate in regional events.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of exercising sound judgment independently, with the credibility to mentor and be sought out by less experienced peers.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred / Nice to Have:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with AI-assisted tools for CRM, call preparation, meeting summaries, or customer data analysis.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of Menlo Security's isolation platform or similar web/email security technologies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in a SaaS or high-growth technology company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in the Asia-Pacific (APAC) region or with Japanese enterprise customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Relevant security certifications (e.g., CISSP, CEH) or formal security training.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience running customer advisory boards, facilitating customer communities, or mentoring junior team members formally.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/\">LinkedIn</a>!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why Menlo?</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: <strong>Proactive Leadership</strong>, <strong>Straight Talk</strong>, <strong>United Impact</strong>, <strong>Elevated Talent</strong>, and <strong>Customer-Compelled</strong>. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability</strong>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>TO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.</strong></em></p>","descriptionPlain":"Menlo Security is the leader in Browser Security for human and agentic workforces. Our mission is to enable humans and agents to connect, communicate, and collaborate securely, without compromise. The Menlo Browser Security Platform protects organizations from cyberattacks by stopping threats across the web, documents, and email before they reach the user. With Menlo Agent Runtime Security (MARS), that protection now extends to the AI agents working alongside every employee. Menlo Security is trusted by major global businesses, including Fortune 500 companies and government agencies, to protect their most valuable asset, their data, and is backed by top-tier investors.\n\n\nSUMMARY\n\nWe're looking for a Senior Customer Success Manager to own the strategic relationship with our largest and most complex enterprise customers across Japan. You'll be the primary point of contact and trusted advisor for your portfolio, working closely with deployment, sales, and engineering teams to ensure customers realize maximum value from Menlo's isolation platform, and you'll be looked to as a source of judgment when accounts get complicated. You'll balance deep technical fluency with business acumen—using AI tools to accelerate account research and customer communication—so you can focus your energy on the strategic conversations that drive retention and expansion. You'll be bilingual in English and Japanese, comfortable traveling to customer sites, and someone junior CSMs can learn from.\n\n\nOUTCOMES & KPIS\n\nKey Outcome(s) Owned:\n\n - Customer retention and net revenue retention (NRR) across a portfolio of strategic, high-complexity accounts\n\n - Successful deployment and adoption of Menlo solutions, with customers reaching their defined value milestones\n\n - Uplift in team-wide execution through mentorship and playbook contributions that other CSMs rely on\n\nSuccess Metrics / KPIs:\n\n - Net retention rate (NRR) and expansion revenue for your book of business\n\n - Customer satisfaction scores and NPS feedback from your accounts (QBRs, surveys, touchpoints)\n\n - Deployment success rate and time-to-value for implementations you support\n\n - Forecast accuracy for customer renewals and expansion opportunities in your portfolio\n\n - Contribution to team enablement: playbooks authored, peers mentored, workshops led\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own the strategic relationship with enterprise customers across Japan, serving as the senior technical advisor and business partner to CTOs, CISOs, Security Architects, and Security Engineers, including at the most complex or highest-visibility accounts in the region.\n\n - Lead quarterly business reviews (QBRs) and executive touchpoints independently, presenting Menlo cloud security assessments with tailored, forward-looking recommendations; use AI-assisted meeting summaries and CRM enrichment to track progress and inform strategy.\n\n - Identify and build the business case for expansion opportunities using data-driven insights and AI-powered account research, and work with sales to convert them into upsell and cross-sell revenue.\n\n - Anticipate deployment and adoption risk before it surfaces; partner with technical teams on system design, configuration, and resiliency, and author or refine the Statements of Work (SOWs) and playbooks that guide implementations across the team.\n\n - Design and deliver region-based workshops and user groups that enable customers on product capabilities, drawing on AI tools to synthesize feedback patterns and relay actionable insight to product and engineering teams.\n\n - Partner cross-functionally with sales and pre-sales leadership to shape account strategy, support renewals, and represent the voice of the Japan customer base in broader planning.\n\n - Establish and maintain working relationships with key regional partners to effectively manage renewal opportunities\n\n\nFUNCTIONAL COMPETENCIES\n\nRequired:\n\n - 8–10+ years of experience in a customer-facing technical role (e.g., Customer Success Manager, Technical Account Manager, Sales Engineer, Solutions Engineer, or equivalent), with a track record on complex, high-value accounts.\n\n - Native or near-native fluency in Japanese (written and verbal), sufficient to read complex contracts or technical documentation and negotiate, present to, and build trust with senior executive stakeholders without relying on translation or simplification\n\n - Professional fluency in English for internal collaboration\n\n - Deep knowledge of network security technologies: proxies, firewalls (NG/traditional), SSL/TLS, IPSec, SSO (SAML, OAuth, LDAP), MDM, Cloud APIs, SIEM, DLP, and CASB gateways.\n\n - Demonstrated success supporting and deploying security solutions for large or high-complexity enterprise customers, including navigating multi-stakeholder, multi-team environments.\n\n - Excellent communication skills and proven comfort presenting to and influencing executive-level audiences.\n\n - Strong project management and organizational skills; able to manage a demanding portfolio and competing priorities without close oversight.\n\n - Willingness to travel to customer sites (up to 30%) and participate in regional events.\n\n - A track record of exercising sound judgment independently, with the credibility to mentor and be sought out by less experienced peers.\n\nPreferred / Nice to Have:\n\n - Experience with AI-assisted tools for CRM, call preparation, meeting summaries, or customer data analysis.\n\n - Knowledge of Menlo Security's isolation platform or similar web/email security technologies.\n\n - Background in a SaaS or high-growth technology company.\n\n - Experience in the Asia-Pacific (APAC) region or with Japanese enterprise customers.\n\n - Relevant security certifications (e.g., CISSP, CEH) or formal security training.\n\n - Experience running customer advisory boards, facilitating customer communities, or mentoring junior team members formally.\n\nFollow us on LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/company/menlo-security/!\n\nWhy Menlo?\n\nAt Menlo, we don't settle for the status quo — in our technology or our culture. How we think and act is just as important as what we build. Our culture is defined by five core mindsets: Proactive Leadership, Straight Talk, United Impact, Elevated Talent, and Customer-Compelled. We take ownership and drive outcomes without waiting to be told. We communicate directly and seek hard truths. We break down silos and win together. We hold a high bar for ourselves and the people around us. And we treat every customer interaction as mission-critical. If you're someone who sees it, owns it, solves it, and does it — you'll thrive here.\n\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, sex, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, or on the basis of disability.\n\nTO ALL AGENCIES: Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Menlo Security outside of the Talent organization. Menlo Security’s policy is to only accept resumes from agencies via Ashby (ATS). Agencies must have a valid services agreement executed and must have been assigned by the Talent team to a specific requisition. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Menlo Security. In the event a candidate submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment will be paid.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}}],"apiVersion":"1"}